{
	chapter.27788EED80A7CD97.title: "Automation Challenges"
	chapter.38D2947EAFF15957.title: "The Beginning"
	chapter.3E6D2AFA5799E080.title: "OriTech"
	quest.00752F7C1626C2A4.quest_subtitle: "You're a Natural (log)!"
	quest.00752F7C1626C2A4.title: "ln"
	quest.01AAB32F8964824B.quest_desc: [
		"Yes, it's the obligatory &6Tech Mod Wrench!&r And just like every other wrench, it can ro-...wait, what's that? I'm getting something from the higher-ups."
		""
		"Yes, uh huh. mhm. Yep. Ok, I see. Alright, talk to you later."
		""
		""
		"Well, it turns out this wrench actually &4can't rotate machines. &rBut that's fine. What the wrench can REALLY do is &aadd/remove connections &rfrom both energy and fluid pipes. By default, the pipes will automatically connect to each other and machines, which can definitely muck things up if your setup is compact. So, you can use this to make sure pipes stay connected to only the pies you want."
	]
	quest.01AAB32F8964824B.quest_subtitle: "So you make a monkey wrench pun despite the wrench OBVIOUSLY being a crescent wrench?"
	quest.01AAB32F8964824B.title: "Monkeying Around"
	quest.02100971DEF8BBB1.quest_desc: ["Use this quest to get an &eunlimited source of torches!"]
	quest.02100971DEF8BBB1.quest_subtitle: "I'm a Torches R Us kid"
	quest.023529219802E248.quest_desc: ["This &5weird goop&r can be created in the Refiner using Lava and Enderic Compound. It doesn't seem to have any adverse effects when taking a dip in it, &zso you can make a swimming pool out of it&r :D"]
	quest.023529219802E248.quest_subtitle: "Never trust Matter: It makes up EVERYTHING!"
	quest.023529219802E248.title: "What's the Matter?"
	quest.02B2DB759A15882C.quest_desc: ["This component is where you insert your &aUranium&r or &dPlutonium&r pellets. These components go on the &2top side&r of the reactor, above the &afuel rods.&r You should put one above each fuel rod or stack of fuel rods (&eremember what I said about being able to duplicate the layout of your reactor vertically?&r)"]
	quest.02B2DB759A15882C.quest_subtitle: "What'll it be, boys? Uranium, or Plutonium?"
	quest.02B2DB759A15882C.title: "Fill 'Er Up"
	quest.033EF248F606214E.quest_desc: [
		"This chungus of a machine can &6infinitely extract&r minerals from bedrock-level &9resource nodes."
		""
		"But how do you find a resource node? Well, in your travels, you might have come across some surface-level &8boulders&r with some ores buried in them. If you dig down to bedrock underneath these boulders, you'll find plenty of resource nodes matching the &5ores present in the boulders."
		""
		"Build the machine over top of as many resource nodes it can reach (the machine is 3x3, so plan carefully). Then, you must use one or more &bEnderic Lasers&r to power it, since there's no place for a power plug. You can then use &6Item Pipes&r to extract the spoils."
	]
	quest.033EF248F606214E.quest_subtitle: "Though since we're using mods, shouldn't it be Modded Extract(or)?"
	quest.033EF248F606214E.title: "Vanilla Extract(or)"
	quest.0344280C26C67DDD.quest_subtitle: "You're being charged right now to read this quest"
	quest.0344280C26C67DDD.title: "Nickel and Dimed"
	quest.03E76C838E6C734D.quest_subtitle: "That's it, there are no more cobblestones in the world. You mined them ALL."
	quest.03E76C838E6C734D.title: "No Stone Unturned"
	quest.04538327F9D1A526.quest_subtitle: "Hello."
	quest.04538327F9D1A526.title: "Jobs Creator"
	quest.058D293601A3149C.quest_subtitle: "Give me what I desire (which is 100B of Light Naphtha)"
	quest.058D293601A3149C.title: "Gimmie Fuel Gimmie Fire"
	quest.05DBCB97A501DD7C.quest_desc: [
		"Mineral Slurry can be used in the Centrifuge with &aBiopolymers/Polymer Resin&r to double your Plastic output (as opposed to using Water)."
		""
		"It can also be used in the Refiner with Clay Catalyst Beads to create Nether Quartz."
	]
	quest.05DBCB97A501DD7C.quest_subtitle: "OINK OINK, EAT UP LITTLE PIGGY"
	quest.05DBCB97A501DD7C.title: "AI Slop"
	quest.06EDF4E5376D7614.quest_subtitle: "You've been VERY BAD this year..."
	quest.06EDF4E5376D7614.title: "Naughty List"
	quest.07BA46094BD213D4.quest_subtitle: "Get with the times"
	quest.07BA46094BD213D4.title: "The Future of Fueling is Now"
	quest.0803641B8A99C6D5.quest_desc: [
		"Light Naptha is a very versatile hydrocarbon with many uses."
		""
		"First, you can &cburn it in a fuel generator, plain and simple.&r"
		""
		"Second, you can &buse it in the Centrifuge&r to create Silicon Wash and Polymer Resin."
		""
		"But probably the most useful use is &6using it in the Refiner with Carbon Strands."
		""
		"Get a bucket of this stuff, and the next quest will talk more about it!"
	]
	quest.0803641B8A99C6D5.quest_subtitle: "Don't eat the grapes grown here. Trust me."
	quest.0803641B8A99C6D5.title: "Naptha Valley"
	quest.0837758320D296E4.quest_desc: [
		"&zYou can trade your Banana for exactly ONE creative Tank.&r"
		""
		"This tank can be filled with &5ANY&r liquid of your choosing."
		""
		"&4BE CAREFUL!&r &cOnce filled, the tank canNOT be emptied. Furthermore, once placed, the tank canNOT be removed or moved.&r"
		""
		"What will you fill it with? Hopefully not water."
	]
	quest.0837758320D296E4.quest_subtitle: "Oceans of fun!"
	quest.0837758320D296E4.title: "An Endless Sea"
	quest.094D4EDB896A2E1C.quest_desc: [
		"&4The granddaddy of energy storage!!!&r"
		""
		"To use this device, you'll need one of many different compatible blocks. &dYou can hold down SHIFT while mousing over the Vault item to view all compatible blocks.&r"
		""
		"Place this block in the world, and click on it while holding the vault to turn it into an Energy Storage device. &6The more dangerous the block, the more energy it can store.&r Aiming Enderic Lasers at the device will increase the amount of energy you can store."
	]
	quest.094D4EDB896A2E1C.quest_subtitle: "Looks like the cat's out of the box...and also still in the box..."
	quest.094D4EDB896A2E1C.title: "Wanted: Dead AND Alive"
	quest.099A8FB38E7474A9.quest_desc: ["For some reason, you can only make this core &anow&r as opposed to the next level core, which you could make before it. That's kind of unbalanced, but I'm not complaining..."]
	quest.099A8FB38E7474A9.quest_subtitle: "Seriously, you can make the Ultra core before this one. That's kinda broken."
	quest.099A8FB38E7474A9.title: "Worse than Ultra?"
	quest.09C9B426DFE7A555.quest_subtitle: "This just in! The economy is in shambles after a local engineer discovered a yet-untapped infinte source of our only currency!"
	quest.09C9B426DFE7A555.title: "Villager Newsworthy"
	quest.09CD3A0C7E45AC2B.quest_desc: [
		"This mod adds certain &9tools and armor&r that require stored &eelectrical charge&r to operate. When you craft these tools, their batteries are dead, so you have to charge them, somehow. This handy-dandy &2wireless charging pad&r can inject some energy into those tools, provided you plug it in first."
		""
		"Wait, hold on...you could make this with a &4Redstone Block&r this whole time??? Aw, geez..."
	]
	quest.09CD3A0C7E45AC2B.quest_subtitle: "How do you stop a rhino from charging? You unplug his phone!"
	quest.09CD3A0C7E45AC2B.title: "CHAAAAAARGE!!!"
	quest.0A2D818CFD7029F4.quest_subtitle: "if you have 10 of them then you have a famous rapper"
	quest.0A2D818CFD7029F4.title: "5 Cent"
	quest.0B37CD887F073E20.quest_desc: [
		"&lHello, hi, Hola, Konnichiwa, greetings, and salutations!!"
		""
		"I would like to formally welcome you to this modpack, &z&lOriTech Academy&r!"
		""
		"To continue, just click that \"checkmark\" in the top left of this window."
		""
		"Oh, by the way...this chapter is all onboarding stuff. It'll also explain some of the utility mods included, and some of the special quirks and permissions I've given you."
	]
	quest.0B37CD887F073E20.quest_subtitle: "We're so glad you're here."
	quest.0BCDEFDCD3BB7A34.quest_desc: ["This is it. The last computer crafting ingredient. I hope you've enjoyed the journey."]
	quest.0BCDEFDCD3BB7A34.quest_subtitle: "No Breaking Bad references here, folks"
	quest.0BCDEFDCD3BB7A34.title: "Heisenberg's Entryway to Matrix Mechanics"
	quest.0C7B7FBF7D6EA1B6.quest_desc: [
		"Many of the machines in OriCraft are &dMultiblock machines,&r which means they require a space of &emore than 1x1&r to operate. All OriCraft machines are born into the world as 1x1 blocks, but some will demand these things called \"machine cores.\""
		""
		"By clicking on a machine that requires &6cores, &ryou can see where you need to place the cores for the machine to expand to its operating form. In fact, if you click the machine with cores in hand, it will &5automatically place a core in one of the correct spots for you."
		""
		"Better cores will improve the operating effiency and power output of your machines, and they will also let you attach more &5upgrade modules &rto that machine. You should be able to make any of the cores listed in this quest with the materials you have access to."
	]
	quest.0C7B7FBF7D6EA1B6.quest_subtitle: "Making your machines turn Inside Out"
	quest.0C7B7FBF7D6EA1B6.title: "Core Memory"
	quest.0C928DFDACB3CB51.quest_desc: ["This addon gives any machine its attached to a HEFTY &6additional energy capacity, &ras well as an increased energy transfer rate."]
	quest.0C928DFDACB3CB51.quest_subtitle: "Thank you, thank you very much"
	quest.0C928DFDACB3CB51.title: "Capacitive Audience"
	quest.0CDA9B59F6DB32F6.quest_desc: ["You'll need these things to create Particle Accelerator motors, as well as to create the Exo Jetpack (a combination Exo-Chestplate and Jetpack)."]
	quest.0CDA9B59F6DB32F6.quest_subtitle: "He died doing the thing he loved...staring down the exhaust end of an Ion Thruster."
	quest.0CDA9B59F6DB32F6.title: "Ionic, Isn't It?"
	quest.0D50F4DCDC132F47.quest_desc: ["This addon applies to the Enderic Laser and the Block Breaker. I think you'll be able to figure out what it does...but if it's not clear, then you can use it to apply Silk Touch to your machines that can break blocks. &aUseful for getting ores to pulverize! (1 ore = 2 raw ores!)&r"]
	quest.0D50F4DCDC132F47.quest_subtitle: "mmmmmmm"
	quest.0D50F4DCDC132F47.title: "Silky Smooth"
	quest.0D7A3720830BA7F4.quest_subtitle: "What's all this Mumbo Jumbo about?"
	quest.0D7A3720830BA7F4.title: "Circuitry Confusion"
	quest.0D8E2B236D918B68.quest_desc: [
		"Have you used the &aPlacer Block&r or the &9Fertilizer&r yet? This machine works &overy similarly&r to that. This machine will break the layer of blocks directly below it. On its own, that's not very useful. However, there are some &bAddons&r that will greatly improve your experience:"
		""
		"- Crop addon: This addon will &askip any unmature crops, &rwhich allows the breaker to ONLY harvest grown crops."
		""
		"- Quarry addon: This addon will allow the breaker to &6dig the area out towards bedrock.&r This is a great way to automatically get lots of resources before you have the Bedrock Extractor."
	]
	quest.0D8E2B236D918B68.quest_subtitle: "Break it down!"
	quest.0D8E2B236D918B68.title: "The Opposite of Create"
	quest.0F8AC04841DA16FE.quest_desc: [
		"When you have Naptha and Carbon Fiber rods, you can finally make Reinforced Carbon Sheets! These sheets can be used to make &bIon Thrusters (needed for Particle Accelerators)&r, or..."
		""
		"You can use them with the &5Atomic Forge&r to create Duratium &aWITHOUT having to use expensive Netherite!&r Finally, you're free from the shackles of endless grinding in the Nether! &zHooray!&r"
	]
	quest.0F8AC04841DA16FE.quest_subtitle: "Actually, carbon fiber is VERY brittle..."
	quest.0F8AC04841DA16FE.title: "Bullet Proof"
	quest.0FC19EDB2AE879EE.quest_desc: [
		"Behold, the &bEnderic Laser!&r This versatile machine can be used to &epower certain machines, &5break blocks, &chunt mobs, &rand most importantly: &d&lgenerate Fluxite.&r"
		""
		"To use the laser, you'll need the &aTargeting Device.&r With the targeting device in hand, just right-click the location you want the laser to target. Then, &6shift-right-click&r the BOTTOM block of the laser (it's a 2-block-tall multiblock) to make the laser point towards that location. Plug the laser in, and it will start shooting out towards your targeted location!"
	]
	quest.0FC19EDB2AE879EE.quest_subtitle: "BWAAAAAHHHHH!!!!"
	quest.0FC19EDB2AE879EE.title: "Imma Firin Mah Lazor"
	quest.10505541E54F694A.quest_desc: ["This chestplate is like having an &aequipment charger&r right in your inventory! Provided you charge &oit&r first, it will keep your electric tools nice and juiced up for long mining expeditions."]
	quest.10505541E54F694A.quest_subtitle: "Everywhere I go...I see his face."
	quest.10505541E54F694A.title: "I Am Iron Man"
	quest.12347A7DE6941B74.quest_desc: [
		"&lWelcome to the Wild World of OriTech!"
		""
		"Unlike a lot of other mods, OriTech adds only &9three&f new ores: &eNickel&f, &bPlatinum&r, and &aUranium."
		""
		"Nickel can be found simply by mining around. You'll discover some eventually."
		""
		"However, &bPlatinum&r and &aUranium&r can only be found at Deepslate Level. However, you don't quite &cneed&r Platinum just yet, and Uranium is technically &5completely optional."
		""
		"Oh, also. You may be wondering where all the quests are. Well, most of them are hidden, to prevent you from being overwhelmed. Once you complete all of a quest's dependencies, it will reveal itself! In the meantime, start by trying to accomplish the &ehexagonal starting tasks."
	]
	quest.12347A7DE6941B74.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to my mine"
	quest.12347A7DE6941B74.title: "Ore-y Tech"
	quest.125C71F7AFC9EF9B.quest_subtitle: "No monkeys were harmed in the making of this quest"
	quest.125C71F7AFC9EF9B.title: "Neurally Linked"
	quest.13138FAB18D27FE5.quest_desc: [
		"This machine will become very useful in setting up an &5automated farm!&r The way to use it is identical to the &6Placer Block, &rthe quest for which can be found directly to the left of this one."
		""
		"The Fertilizer requires only &eelectricity &rand &9water&r or &bmineral slurry&r to operate. Once you connect it to a rectangle made out of &6machine frames&r (hint: you can use the same frame you used for your Block Placer Machine), it will spawn a little &5gantry&r and begin to go to work."
		""
		"The fertilizer will:"
		"- Keep farmland&9 hydrated&r, meaning there's no need for water blocks in your fields."
		"- Apply a &2slight growth boost&r to each crop it passes over. It's not as strong as bonemeal, but it's still enough to have a farm go much faster than normal!"
		""
		"Hint: You can have &amultiple&r fertilizers hooked up to the same machine frame to &2greatly accelerate growth!&r 7 is enough for each wheat growth stage."
	]
	quest.13138FAB18D27FE5.quest_subtitle: "Irrigation Irritation"
	quest.13138FAB18D27FE5.title: "Robo-Watering Can"
	quest.134E91EFF161BD45.quest_subtitle: "Join the Rod Squad"
	quest.134E91EFF161BD45.title: "Rod Refresher"
	quest.14AE515086D0FF43.quest_subtitle: "Pearls before girls"
	quest.14AE515086D0FF43.title: "Ender Dispenser"
	quest.1502FBEB411F02B6.quest_desc: [
		"This is basically an electric smelter. Any recipe that can be done in a furnace can also be done in here."
		""
		"So why would you use this? Well, since it runs on &eelectricity,  &ris doesn't need any &ccoal, at least not directly."
		""
		"Additionally, you can attach &5upgrade modules&r to the bottom of it to increase the speed and energy efficiency. With a bunch of these, you can absolutely BLAZE through stacks of smeltables in no time flat!"
	]
	quest.1502FBEB411F02B6.quest_subtitle: "A lean mean oven machine"
	quest.1502FBEB411F02B6.title: "Smelter Skelter"
	quest.153894C950033695.quest_desc: [
		"In addition to regular pipes, there are also &6framed versions&r of each one. Unlike ducts, these will still auto-snap to machines, meaning you'll have to use a wrench to get rid of unneeded connections."
		""
		"There are framed versions of &6item pipes, &9fluid pipes, &4energy pipes, &band superconductors."
	]
	quest.153894C950033695.quest_subtitle: "I've been...FRAMED!!!"
	quest.153894C950033695.title: "I Didn't Do It!"
	quest.15839FCC37A01DB7.quest_desc: ["With &5Enderic Compound &runder your belt, you can now afford to make one more tier of core! Remember, using higher tier cores means the machine will be more efficient, and can handle more &9addons!"]
	quest.15839FCC37A01DB7.quest_subtitle: "This core is a descendant of the previous cores"
	quest.15839FCC37A01DB7.title: "Rotten to the Core"
	quest.16021491CCEE0C92.quest_desc: ["Once you've got your Enderic Laser, it's time to go &dExploring!&r \"Exploring for what?\", you may ask. Well, we're looking for &5Underground Amethyst Geodes. &rWhen Budding Amethyst is subjected to high-power Enderic Laser beams, it both &astimulates growth&r and transforms it into a mysterious NEW material called &dFluxite.&r Use your &atargeting device&r to target the budding amethyst block, then &5shift-right-click&r the bottom block of the Enderic Laser to set its target. Plug it in, and it'll go to work!"]
	quest.16021491CCEE0C92.quest_subtitle: "Wibbly Wobbly"
	quest.16021491CCEE0C92.title: "In a State of Flux"
	quest.16F7894785EC8434.quest_subtitle: "I think I can"
	quest.16F7894785EC8434.title: "The Little Engine That Could"
	quest.1709089BCB92F885.quest_desc: [
		"This machine allows you to &aplace down blocks automatically!&r Its main use will be part of a &dfully automatic farm!&r Here's how to use it:"
		""
		"-Build a flat rectangle (as big as you want) out of &6Machine Frames&r (they're showcased in the quest after this one)."
		"- Place this machine such that it connects to the rectangle."
		"- Provide this machine &eelectricity &rand the &6block or item you want it to place."
		"- The machine will spawn a little &5gantry&r and start placing whatever you gave it!"
		""
		"How can we use this as part of a farm? Well, if you give it &aseeds,&r it will automatically place the seeds onto tilled soil. You don't have anything yet that can automatically harvest the crops, but it's a start!"
	]
	quest.1709089BCB92F885.quest_subtitle: "Take me home, country roads, to the place, I belong"
	quest.1709089BCB92F885.title: "There's No Place(r) Like Home"
	quest.174CB6EA406B8C4B.quest_desc: [
		"It looks like this &atech mod&r has a little bit of &5magic&r in it! Oh well, it's only a LITTLE bit, so let's learn how to use it!"
		""
		"This machine operates using &5souls. &rWhenever a mob dies near it, its soul will be drawn towards its internal &5soul collection chamber.&r From there, you can use a &dmax-level enchanted book&r to enchant a tool as many times as you want, provided the arcane has enough souls."
		""
		"If you aim an &bEnderic Laser&r at the arcane, you can &astore MORE souls&r in it, which allows you to &bhypercharge&r your tools. Be warned, though. If the laser goes offline while there are more than 50 souls in storage, &csomething BAD will happen..."
	]
	quest.174CB6EA406B8C4B.quest_subtitle: "Everybody wants to be my enemy"
	quest.174CB6EA406B8C4B.title: "Oh, The Misery"
	quest.177CD5F4378558FA.quest_desc: [
		"Time to get into arguably the &5coolest aspect&r of this mod: &eParticle Accelerators!"
		""
		"Particle Accelerators are capable of accelerating items to INSANE speeds, and then colliding them together to form new items, and cause some &oweird things&r to happen."
		""
		"I'll use these quests to explain as much as I can, but if you have some trouble wrapping your head around some of this, I recommend consulting the OriTech Mod Documentation for the Particle Accelerator, which can be accessed by &dclicking the little link icon&r below this quest. You can also hold down &6alt&r while mousing over certain items to open up an in-game wiki."
	]
	quest.177CD5F4378558FA.quest_subtitle: "Perfect Rotation!"
	quest.17AC80A46BE0EA98.quest_desc: [
		"This works a bit differently from the regular &6Arcane.&r Instead of directly consuming &5souls, &rit consumes &eelectricity.&r Additionally, you'll need&9 multiple Arcanes&r nearby, stocked with souls."
		""
		"Wait, &5souls?&r Why use this machine, then? Well, with this machine, you can &achoose which enchantment you want.&r You'll need a lot more souls, and of course a lot of Arcanes, so you might want to get a &6mob farm&r or &9Soul Flower farm&r going."
	]
	quest.17AC80A46BE0EA98.quest_subtitle: "You aren't ready for it yet, but your kids are gonna love it"
	quest.17AC80A46BE0EA98.title: "Enchantment Under The Sea"
	quest.185922D44DF60A6B.quest_subtitle: "Come with me if you want to not die"
	quest.185922D44DF60A6B.title: "T1000"
	quest.1859E1593DFC694A.quest_desc: [
		"This component is one of two ways of &bcooling your reactor.&r This is the &2active method&r of cooling. You need to place a &bcoolant absorber port&r above each stack of coolant absorbers in order for it to work. Then, use whichever method you want to insert &bice blocks&r into the port."
		""
		"But wait, how can you make ice? Perhaps the &9Industrial Chiller&r would be of use..."
	]
	quest.1859E1593DFC694A.quest_subtitle: "CoolantBob AbsorberPants!"
	quest.1859E1593DFC694A.title: "Absorbant and Blue and Maybe Porus is He"
	quest.188A56D2F660EC26.quest_desc: ["I know you were expecting something like &4storage drawers&r or something similar. However, to keep this modpack light and simple, I've chosen &9Iron Chests&r instead. You can use upgrades similar to this one to upgrade your chests to have more storage space, plain and simple. &6First one's on the house!&r"]
	quest.188A56D2F660EC26.quest_subtitle: "I hope you like chests!!!"
	quest.18CF7A18FE186EDC.quest_desc: [
		"Here are the colors of the minerals you can find:"
		""
		"- &4Red: Redstone"
		"- &0Black: Coal"
	]
	quest.18CF7A18FE186EDC.quest_subtitle: "In reality...there are only two."
	quest.18CF7A18FE186EDC.title: "8 Essential Vitamins and Minerals"
	quest.192163FD98FA85F7.quest_desc: ["You may think this &adrill&r will let you mine a larger area at once, but you'll have to wait until you get &6Promethium &rfor that. But, at least you have a pickaxe and shovel that's fast, won't break, and can be recharged!"]
	quest.192163FD98FA85F7.quest_subtitle: "'Cause I got that DRILLERRRRRR, DRILLERRRRR NIGHT"
	quest.192163FD98FA85F7.title: "Drill Seeker"
	quest.196B51947A79AEF1.quest_subtitle: "Ba da ba bap bah"
	quest.196B51947A79AEF1.title: "I'm Lovin' It"
	quest.198D760527EF154D.quest_desc: ["This addon applies to the &6Block Destroyer.&r Essentially, it turns it into an automated hole digger. If you remember the &eBuildcraft Quarry,&r it works similarly to that. The hardness of the block will affect the time it takes to break, but you can mitigate this by using &2lots of speed addons!&r Just make sure you have enough power...and don't forget to connect the Block Destroyer to a chest to hold all the loot!"]
	quest.198D760527EF154D.quest_subtitle: "Close enough, welcome back Buildcraft"
	quest.198D760527EF154D.title: "The Big Dig"
	quest.19D206DFC0C77C33.quest_subtitle: "Stop! You've violated the law!"
	quest.19D206DFC0C77C33.title: "You'll Never Catch Me, Copper!"
	quest.1A4DAF474090468E.quest_desc: ["In your travels, especially those to the &edesert,&r you might come across some spouts of black liquid. This is sweet, sweet, crude oil. Underneath those spouts are large &5underground pockets&r of the stuff. Oil can be pumped out using a &apump.&r Use a bucket to collect the top spout, and then place the pump over the ground-level hole filled with oil."]
	quest.1A4DAF474090468E.quest_subtitle: "EFF YEAH!!!!!"
	quest.1A4DAF474090468E.title: "'MURICA"
	quest.1A5B43E24089FC3D.quest_desc: ["This monster of a generator can burn a variety of fuels to generate lots of power! Oil, Diesel, and Turbofuel are among the liquids you can put in there."]
	quest.1A5B43E24089FC3D.quest_subtitle: "POWERRRRRRRRR!!!!!"
	quest.1A5B43E24089FC3D.title: "V10"
	quest.1B565AFD06A7315C.quest_subtitle: "Better watch out or she'll take your cash"
	quest.1B565AFD06A7315C.title: "She's Dangerous, Super Bad"
	quest.1D74CF559D8E0F71.quest_subtitle: "I just couldn't resist."
	quest.1D74CF559D8E0F71.title: "When the Bad is Breaking"
	quest.1DBECD12B2756067.quest_subtitle: "FYI: Automated enchanting in this mod does NOT use lapis."
	quest.1DBECD12B2756067.title: "Unlimited Power"
	quest.1EBE0E68E895C46F.quest_desc: ["This little thing is the &ckey&r to creating a VERY important machine: &bThe Enderic Laser."]
	quest.1EBE0E68E895C46F.quest_subtitle: "You still probably shouldn't stare at it."
	quest.1EBE0E68E895C46F.title: "Class 1M"
	quest.1F24A00D2A4400D3.quest_subtitle: "It's like an action moo-vie"
	quest.1F24A00D2A4400D3.title: "Raisin' the Steaks"
	quest.1F3D1E0D93767161.quest_desc: [
		"&zYou can trade TWO bananas for exactly ONE Creative Energy Storage."
		"&r"
		"This will function as an &5INFINITE&r source of power."
		""
		"&4BE CAREFUL!&r &cOnce placed, you canNOT remove it.&r"
		""
		"What will YOU power with this?"
		""
		"...But wait...you only got one Banana. &zHow can you get another Banana?&r"
	]
	quest.1F3D1E0D93767161.quest_subtitle: "We are not affiliated with TheFatRat in any way."
	quest.1F3D1E0D93767161.title: "Infinite Power"
	quest.1FFEDF5645667F66.quest_desc: ["Liquid Tasks are completed just like regular tasks, but you have to pipe in liquids to the Task screen instead of funneling in items."]
	quest.1FFEDF5645667F66.quest_subtitle: "Splish Sploosh"
	quest.1FFEDF5645667F66.title: "Liquid Tasks"
	quest.2003C472A9B4656A.quest_desc: ["Diesel can be burned in the Fuel Generator for electricity, or you can use it in the Centrifuge with Fluxite to create Turbofuel (which can ALSO be burned in the Fuel Gen for electricity). &eBasically, it's destined to be burned one way or another."]
	quest.2003C472A9B4656A.quest_subtitle: "EPA TEST DETECTED. EFFICIENCY MODE ACTIVATED."
	quest.2003C472A9B4656A.title: "Emissions Scandal"
	quest.204449D02CFBB2DF.quest_desc: [
		"All these other generators I've talked about can produce lots of power, but how about we produce &eMORE????"
		""
		"Introducing the &aNuclear Reactor!&r This massive machine can produce a TON of power, but you've gotta fuel it with a steady supply of &aUranium Pellets&r as well as coolant."
		""
		"Reactors are &emodular, &rand can be built in a lot of different configurations. In these tutorial quests, I'll be going over what the different parts do and where to put them, but you are highly encouraged to consult the &dofficial OriTech Documentation&r by clicking the little link icon next to this quest (which unlocks after you make the controller)"
	]
	quest.204449D02CFBB2DF.quest_subtitle: "And I would walk 3 more"
	quest.204449D02CFBB2DF.title: "And I Would Walk 3 Miles"
	quest.2078BC6919DC4082.quest_desc: [
		"You will most &ocertainly &rneed a way to shuttle items around your factories, and this is where the &aitem pipe &rcomes in!"
		""
		"This item pipe works in a very specific way. It will attempt to &apush &ritems into the &4closest connected non-full inventory&r up to 256 blocks away. This means you may have to get clever with how you route your items. If you want a pipe to extract from an inventory, just &aclick on it!&r &cBy default, the pipe will ONLY extract from the first slot in the connected inventory.&r &6Right-clicking the pipe with a Motor will let it extract from the whole inventory.&r"
		""
		"There are certain upgrades/tools you can use to make your life with item pipes easier, which you'll discover later on down the line."
	]
	quest.2078BC6919DC4082.quest_subtitle: "Let's-a-go!"
	quest.2078BC6919DC4082.title: "World 1-1"
	quest.209970865CCA1F4D.quest_desc: [
		"We're about to make the Refiner, a machine that can take certain items and liquids and turn them into other items and liquids. &6But first, you have to make some Refinery Chamber Modules.&r"
		""
		"These modules are important for crafting the refiner itself, but they're also necessary for optimizing your refiner. You'll learn more about what these tanks do in the next quest."
	]
	quest.209970865CCA1F4D.quest_subtitle: "Why yes I DO like poop and pee jokes"
	quest.209970865CCA1F4D.title: "A Refined Sense of Humor"
	quest.20C3A297D53A97EF.quest_desc: ["Instead of having different tiers of pipes, there is just &cone tier.&r The transfer speed of the default tier should be fast enough for most usage, but should you want faster transport, you can use a &5pipe booster. &rPlace it next to a pipe that is currently EXTRACTING things, and it will automatically latch on. When you provide it with power, it will boost the transfer speed of all connected pipes. This does &4not&r work on Energy Pipes. For that, you'll need to use a &bSuperconductor..."]
	quest.20C3A297D53A97EF.quest_subtitle: "Pfizer or Moderna?"
	quest.20C3A297D53A97EF.title: "Booster Shot"
	quest.2119455E26D52844.quest_subtitle: "The hit song by Imagine Ender Dragons"
	quest.2119455E26D52844.title: "I'm Redstone Active"
	quest.21A38432E81DC6DB.quest_subtitle: "*Bzzzz bzzzz* Knight to A6"
	quest.21A38432E81DC6DB.title: "Stockfish"
	quest.21AB5CB7AC786269.quest_desc: [
		"Finally, something for your &5long-distance logistical needs!&r The Drone Port requires two of them to be really useful. You'll also probably need some &9chunk loaders&r (Remember those? From the onboarding tutorial?) to load the chunks each port is in."
		""
		"To use the drone port, you'll need the &aTargeting Device. &rSimply shift-right-click on the destination drone port with the device, and then insert the device into &9the slot in the source drone port.&r When provided with power, the drone will deliver to the destination when the inventory is not full."
		""
		"Note that &amultple drones can deliver to the same port, &cbut each drone can only deliver to one port."
	]
	quest.21AB5CB7AC786269.quest_subtitle: "Ya like jazz?"
	quest.21AB5CB7AC786269.title: "Busy Little Bees"
	quest.21FDE923D009DFBA.quest_subtitle: "CHOOOOOO CHOOOOO!!!"
	quest.21FDE923D009DFBA.title: "Chugga Chugga"
	quest.220DD9A4BFAE0206.quest_desc: ["This an important gadget that's used with the &bEnderic Laser. &rTo use it, just right-click the location you want save to the targeter, and then shift-right-click &rthe bottom block of the Laser to make the laser target that block. It's as simple as that!"]
	quest.220DD9A4BFAE0206.quest_subtitle: "Are you still there?"
	quest.220DD9A4BFAE0206.title: "Target Acquired"
	quest.227ADBACC8DB4C08.quest_desc: ["The Machine frame is used to mark the &6working area&r for the Fertilizer, Block Placer, and Block Breaker. The only requirements are that it's a &csquare or a rectangle&r that is flat. It can be as big as you want, or even as small as you want. Might be useful in conjunction with the &atree saw&r to create an automated Lumber farm. You can place a 3x3 ring of these thingies, then connect a Block Placer up to it, then use some Filtering magic to route the saplings into the Block Placer. You can then hook up a Fertilizer to automatically water the tree to make it grow faster. Then, the tree saw will automatically cut down the grown tree, and the cycle repeats."]
	quest.227ADBACC8DB4C08.quest_subtitle: "I was...wait. crap. we've already done this joke."
	quest.227ADBACC8DB4C08.title: "I Didn't Do It!"
	quest.227D1CCDFEFB2EFA.quest_subtitle: "Our Combined strength is over like a zillion"
	quest.227D1CCDFEFB2EFA.title: "Past the Thresh-hold"
	quest.232C18A079C53CBB.quest_subtitle: "I made this joke in my OTHER modpack"
	quest.232C18A079C53CBB.title: "Wood in the Morning"
	quest.23AB6A1560B84EC0.quest_desc: [
		"Need a place to store your &9fluids?&r This tank has you covered. You can insert and extract liquids using fluid pipes, as well as manually using buckets and the tank's GUI."
		""
		"Also, they can stack! When you place a tank on top of another tank, the upper one will drain into the lower one!"
	]
	quest.23AB6A1560B84EC0.quest_subtitle: "Tanks for the memories"
	quest.23AB6A1560B84EC0.title: "Think Tank"
	quest.23AC40343D554C09.quest_subtitle: "<Insert CaseOh joke here>"
	quest.23AC40343D554C09.title: "The Garden of Eatin'"
	quest.244EDDB249BD4BB3.quest_desc: ["This machine addon allows the machine to process an additional recipe during an operation cycle. For instance, instead of a pulverizer processing one ore block at a time, it'll process two."]
	quest.244EDDB249BD4BB3.quest_subtitle: "*Blewtewth Mode*"
	quest.244EDDB249BD4BB3.title: "Auxiliary Mode"
	quest.253AEBC87F17C31A.quest_desc: ["This &bBeautiful Blue Ingot&r is made by alloying together &bdiamonds&r and &enickel.&r You'll use it often within these next stages of the game, so now might be a good time to go Diamond hunting! "]
	quest.253AEBC87F17C31A.quest_subtitle: "How X-citing."
	quest.253AEBC87F17C31A.title: "Wolverine"
