	quest.39585D87A3BA3D96.quest_subtitle: "Defying gravity"
	quest.39585D87A3BA3D96.title: "Follow the Yellow Brick Road"
	quest.39682F7807BF3405.quest_desc: ["It's like a regular Energy Storage, but with much more capacity! Like before, &cred plugs are outputs, &agreen plugs are inputs, &bblue plugs are addon slots. "]
	quest.39682F7807BF3405.quest_subtitle: "Nanananananana"
	quest.39682F7807BF3405.title: "Battman"
	quest.3A1C66277BC493B7.quest_subtitle: "Hey, I just met you...and this is CRAZY"
	quest.3A1C66277BC493B7.title: "Coal Me Maybe"
	quest.3A5A83A4436B7CE4.quest_subtitle: "Delicious!!!"
	quest.3A5A83A4436B7CE4.title: "Flesh Factory"
	quest.3A6171B703644AF2.quest_desc: ["You get the best of both worlds with this piece of gear!"]
	quest.3A6171B703644AF2.quest_subtitle: "Props if you rember this gem of a Lego theme"
	quest.3A6171B703644AF2.title: "Exo-Force"
	quest.3BAD63536537CC98.quest_desc: [
		"There are three generators with addon slots: the Biogenerator, the Lava Generator, and the Fuel Generator. By using this &bsteam addon, &ryou can generate some additional electricity, at the cost of setting up some additional infrastructure."
		""
		"Attach this addon to one of the three generators mentioned. Then, you can use Fluid Pipes to pump in water and extract steam."
	]
	quest.3BAD63536537CC98.quest_subtitle: "Smoke? Oh, no, that isn't smoke. It's steam! Steam from the Steam Generator! MMMMMM, Steam Generator!!"
	quest.3BAD63536537CC98.title: "Steam Machine"
	quest.3C76DEA48925A3D1.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations!!!! You've actually done it!!! Of course, your journey &aisn't over yet,&r unless you want it to be. That's right, if you've felt like you've explored the mod enough, you can call it quits right here."
		""
		"...however, if you want to continue, why not try completing the &9Automation Challenges?&r To accomplish those, you'll need to greatly improve your infrastructure, create more machines, and ramp up extraction and logistics. The choice is yours! See how far you can get! Or take a long-deserved rest."
		""
		"&e...Say, is that a Banana? I bet it's really tasty!&r"
	]
	quest.3C76DEA48925A3D1.quest_subtitle: "Congrats! You did it!"
	quest.3C76DEA48925A3D1.title: "Certificate of Completion!"
	quest.3C972757117AA7B0.quest_desc: [
		"&zOoooh...BANANA!!!!&r"
		""
		"...but what is it used for?"
	]
	quest.3C972757117AA7B0.quest_subtitle: "This will take you forever."
	quest.3C972757117AA7B0.title: "Eagle-Eyed"
	quest.3D39991F6A09FD06.quest_desc: [
		"&4Wait, what if I'm in an area that doesn't have Oak Saplings?&r"
		""
		"Well, unfortunately, NeoForge does not have the \"Item Filters\" mod which allows modpack makers to allow you to submit one of many different items. To prevent there from being quests for each and every type of wood, I've just made it so you need Oak wood for the quests. Why oak? Well, it's because they also drop &cApples,&r so you can get started on the Apple quests as well!"
	]
	quest.3D39991F6A09FD06.quest_subtitle: "You can't reap what you don't sow"
	quest.3D39991F6A09FD06.title: "Let it Grow"
	quest.3DC4685E36BD02C7.quest_subtitle: "Well, Seymour, you are an odd fellow...but I must say, you steam a good ham."
	quest.3DC4685E36BD02C7.title: "Unforgettable Luncheon"
	quest.3E2B77AE66200F44.quest_subtitle: "I Lava You Too"
	quest.3E2B77AE66200F44.title: "I Lava You"
	quest.3E35037205B5E4C0.quest_desc: ["The &6centrifuge&r will get you this far on its own, but in order to perform certain crucial recipes, you'll need to add some &9water&r to the mix. For that, you'll need the Fluid Addon. Simply plug it into the &bblue addon port&r on the back of the centrifuge, and right-click the centrifuge to make it recognize the addon. Then, you can pipe water (or other fluids) in through the addon, or you can insert them manually through the centrifuge GUI."]
	quest.3E35037205B5E4C0.quest_subtitle: "AKA the BEST WiiWare game of all time"
	quest.3E35037205B5E4C0.title: "Fluidity"
	quest.3F9EC5ED10715A8C.quest_desc: [
		"There might come a time where you want to do some &6advanced item routing.&r For this, you might want to use a &5filter.&r This block's GUI will let you whitelist (or blacklist) up to 10 different items that can be &4pushed &rinto it (you hear that? You can't use it to PULL items)."
		""
		"You might want to use this to route seeds to your automated farm's &ablock placer, &ror to route saplings to a tree farm's block placer."
	]
	quest.3F9EC5ED10715A8C.quest_subtitle: "Think before you say"
	quest.3F9EC5ED10715A8C.title: "#NoFilter"
	quest.40EB9E555196DC84.quest_desc: ["Similar to the Capacitor Addon, this will also give connected machines an additional energy capacity, but it also functions as some extra ports to attach &badditional machine addons."]
	quest.40EB9E555196DC84.quest_subtitle: "I'm banking on your success"
	quest.40EB9E555196DC84.title: "Ankers Away!"
	quest.412B2A3B67466975.quest_desc: [
		"This addon applies to both the &bEnderic laser&r and the &6Block Destroyer."
		""
		"When applied to the Enderic Laser and combined with the Hunter Addon, the laser will no longer target &6baby animals, &rmeaning they can have a chance to grow up before being &4ethically erased from this plane."
		""
		"When applied to the Block Destroyer, the destroyer will &aonly destroy fully-grown crops.&r. Make sure to attach and activate the addon before energizing your Block Destroyer!"
	]
	quest.412B2A3B67466975.quest_subtitle: "Bro, we're gonna starve"
	quest.412B2A3B67466975.title: "Bad Crop?"
	quest.41AD2E92E1008900.quest_subtitle: "It's charming now, I swear!"
	quest.41AD2E92E1008900.title: "Pt Cruiser"
	quest.41C83752E1F44123.quest_desc: ["Well, here it is. The &6last tier of machine core.&r With these, you'll be able to equip your machines with the &amax amount of addons."]
	quest.41C83752E1F44123.quest_subtitle: "Not really because you can do EVERYTHING here."
	quest.41C83752E1F44123.title: "An Ultimatum"
	quest.41D4CCEE130571F1.quest_subtitle: "Paint"
	quest.41D4CCEE130571F1.title: "Problem Solventer"
	quest.420C2D3C2BDF6126.quest_subtitle: "We are mining diamonds"
	quest.420C2D3C2BDF6126.title: "Welcome to My Mine"
	quest.422B936EE65A7189.quest_subtitle: "I had this one as a kid, you know. They just don't make 'em like this anymore."
	quest.422B936EE65A7189.title: "Lego Set 10194"
	quest.4240E5C666DB4292.quest_desc: ["Wrapping some Nickel around a steel rod will produce a Magnetic Coil. When an electric current is put through it, a magnetic field is produced, which can drive a motor! And as such, this component is &6essential in Motor production! "]
	quest.4240E5C666DB4292.quest_subtitle: "Hey, I just met you (and this is CRAZY)"
	quest.4240E5C666DB4292.title: "Coil Me Maybe"
	quest.435FC20752D22449.quest_subtitle: "We came for the half-life, we stayed for our whole lives"
	quest.435FC20752D22449.title: "Ride The Cyclone"
	quest.43A6384329FAEBDF.quest_desc: [
		"While you're off exploring, you probably want your machines to continue to work, right? Well, when you get too far away from them, they'll &4stop working&r because the chunks they occupy get unloaded. To alleviate this, I've thrown in this nice and simple &aChunk Loaders&r mod for your convenience. This one I gave you for free can load a single chunk, but there are more that can load larger areas. Their recipes are...&6relatively cheap."
		""
		"Oh, and did you know you can press F3 + G to view the chunk borders? This is helpful for &2optimizing your loaders!"
	]
	quest.43A6384329FAEBDF.quest_subtitle: "I think Moto Moto likes you"
	quest.43A6384329FAEBDF.title: "I Like 'Em Chunky"
	quest.43DEEC4B80597E4F.quest_desc: [
		"You've got the machines, you've got the generator, but how do you transfer power? Well, you use &eEnergy Pipes!"
		""
		"Energy pipes will &dautomatically&r connect to a machine and to other energy pipes. You can use a &6pipe wrench&r to get rid of any unneeded connections. Some machines have dedicated energy input/output ports, but for the most part you can just &epush energy in wherever.&r"
	]
	quest.43DEEC4B80597E4F.quest_subtitle: "Tell me what's on your mind"
	quest.43DEEC4B80597E4F.title: "Pure Energy"
	quest.44BBC6D29C5C1231.quest_desc: [
		"This piece isn't necessary for a good accelerator, but you might want to use it to &aautomate the release of particles&r once they've achieved a suitable speed."
		""
		"When you place a &cRedstone Comparator&r with the two torches facing the sensor, it will output a redstone signal proportional to how fast the particle is moving. You can use this to automatically release the particle onto a larger ring or to a collision chamber once it gets up to speed."
	]
	quest.44BBC6D29C5C1231.quest_subtitle: "Do you know how fast you were going back there?"
	quest.44BBC6D29C5C1231.title: "Speed Trap"
	quest.451D8156258F3947.quest_desc: ["The Assembler is another multiblock machine similar to the &6Foundry. &rIt can assemble components using up to &afour ingredients. &rYou'll need it to craft more advanced things like &9 computer chips."]
	quest.451D8156258F3947.quest_subtitle: "CONGREGATE!!!"
	quest.451D8156258F3947.title: "Avengers..."
	quest.4543D00C9FBA5DD4.quest_subtitle: "Kingot? That's the best joke you could come up with?"
	quest.4543D00C9FBA5DD4.title: "Kingot of Ingots"
	quest.457DA7404DFF945E.quest_subtitle: "A cruel twist of fate"
	quest.457DA7404DFF945E.title: "Oh, the Irony"
	quest.458AEA64FA9A07A4.quest_subtitle: "To this day I still don't really remember how to do those"
	quest.458AEA64FA9A07A4.title: "Convolution Confusion"
	quest.45AC7E92D87A68DE.quest_desc: ["Once you have the &6Pulverizer &rand the &eCentrifuge, &ryou can make Carbon Fiber Strands (or Carbon Fibre, for you Bri'ish people out there). These are another crafting component, and you'll need to pulverize coal into coal dust before centrifuging it."]
	quest.45AC7E92D87A68DE.quest_subtitle: "Look how LIGHT they are!"
	quest.45AC7E92D87A68DE.title: "Formula None"
	quest.463D88F05924612C.quest_subtitle: "FREEDOM FOR ALLLLLLL"
	quest.463D88F05924612C.title: "Destiny Manifested"
	quest.465125BB7B3C1D6D.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to HELL"
	quest.465125BB7B3C1D6D.title: "The Worst Rocket League Rank"
	quest.475AF138B907D328.quest_subtitle: "Do you ever think about what happens to the starter pokemon that DOESN'T get chosen?"
	quest.475AF138B907D328.title: "Professor Oak"
	quest.47BDF5BE45ED1C75.quest_desc: [
		"You might have noticed these &bBlue Socket-looking thingies&r on most of the machines. These are &6upgrade slots!&r Depending on what type of cores make up a machine, you can place a certain amount of &aaddon upgrades &rwhich can increase a machine's speed, efficiency, and yield."
		""
		"This block in particular allows you to physically attach more upgrades to a machine, but it doesn't increase the amount of upgrades the machine can use. Remember, that's dependent on the &9cores!"
	]
	quest.47BDF5BE45ED1C75.quest_subtitle: "Why be YOU when you can be NEW???"
	quest.47BDF5BE45ED1C75.title: "Upgrades, people! Upgrades!"
	quest.4948E0DA68E80A0E.quest_desc: [
		"This addon might not seem very useful, but it might have a place in some advanced automation setups. Maybe you'll find a use for it, who knows?"
		""
		"Clicking on the addon itself allows you to configure various modes which are useful when used in conjunction with a comparator."
	]
	quest.4948E0DA68E80A0E.quest_subtitle: "We're gonna bring you home"
	quest.4948E0DA68E80A0E.title: "Ground Control to Major Tom"
	quest.49CC2BEA8B9107D9.quest_desc: [
		"When fuel rods are active, they'll generate &6heat.&r If the heat buildup is too much, your reactor will go &4CRITICAL, &rand you &4don't want to be there when that happens.&r"
		""
		"To prevent this from happening, you'll need to reroute the heat from your rods somewhere using heat pipes. These heat pipes should be connected to either &8heat vents&r or &9heat absorbers."
	]
	quest.49CC2BEA8B9107D9.quest_subtitle: "Bew Bew Bew"
	quest.49CC2BEA8B9107D9.title: "Warp Zone"
	quest.49F93844CC5D5B70.quest_subtitle: "Are...are we SURE this doesn't have any adverse effects?"
	quest.49F93844CC5D5B70.title: "Wibbly Wobbly"
	quest.49FFBD982CFCCD2A.quest_desc: ["I think you know the drill. This is a crafting ingredient. I'm not sure why I feel pressured to write a description for every single quest in this tree."]
	quest.49FFBD982CFCCD2A.quest_subtitle: "AI'm impressed by how far you've come"
	quest.49FFBD982CFCCD2A.title: "ChatGPT"
	quest.4A00FF7EACA16A8E.quest_subtitle: "KNIFE!!!"
	quest.4A00FF7EACA16A8E.title: "Hey. Hey. Hey, Apple. Hey! Hey, Apple!"
	quest.4A55BFEA8399802A.quest_subtitle: "If you tape an apple to a doctor will the universe implode?"
	quest.4A55BFEA8399802A.title: "Doctor's Enemy"
	quest.4A8A4A2CC0B78378.quest_subtitle: "Later, tater!"
	quest.4A8A4A2CC0B78378.title: "Taters Gonna Tate"
	quest.4B295C3C7C880F6E.quest_desc: ["This advanced battery can be used to make some neat things, like&6 jetpacks!"]
	quest.4B295C3C7C880F6E.quest_subtitle: "DINGUS!!!!!"
	quest.4B295C3C7C880F6E.title: "Oh, My PKCell"
	quest.4C4C27ABFFD4D4BF.quest_subtitle: "Cha cha cha Chicken"
	quest.4C4C27ABFFD4D4BF.title: "La la la Lava"
	quest.4D156B49CCAFC0C5.quest_desc: ["Take to the skies with this nifty &6Jetpack!!!&r It requires either &eelectricity&r or &9turbofuel&r to fly."]
	quest.4D156B49CCAFC0C5.quest_subtitle: "Half a Brick is better than none"
	quest.4D156B49CCAFC0C5.title: "Jetpack Joyride"
	quest.4D6E6DDB6798E2FF.quest_desc: [
		"It's time to make one of our first machines: The &9pulverizer."
		""
		"The pulverizer's main job is to grind and mash things up. I think you'll find it most useful in increasing the amount of ore you get from a mining trip. If you put a raw ore chunk in there and provide power, it will output a &6smeltable ore dust&r, &oas well as potentially up to 3 mini-dusts.&r These mini-dusts can be combined together into one full dust, meaning you'll get some bonus ingots from every set of raw ore!"
		""
		"Oh, and here's a useful hint. In your inventory, &2pressing \"U\" while hovering over a machine&r will tell you all the recipes that machine can do. Very useful for discovering the full potential of your tools!"
	]
	quest.4D6E6DDB6798E2FF.quest_subtitle: "Mister Mashy"
	quest.4D6E6DDB6798E2FF.title: "Dream Crusher"
	quest.4DEA8B63D419D985.quest_subtitle: "Well? Get on with it already!"
	quest.4DEA8B63D419D985.title: "Water You Waiting For?"
	quest.4E2600E26A8274DD.quest_subtitle: "Kaboom? Yes, Rico. Kaboom."
	quest.4E2600E26A8274DD.title: "Gunpowder Giver"
	quest.4E4C0D8ECF5AA370.quest_desc: [
		"Rise and shine, because it's &2time to collide!"
		""
		"To collide particles, you'll actually need &5two accelerators, &rbecause each accelerator can only accelerate one particle at a time. What you'll want to do is use the aforementioned &edouble-ring system&r I mentioned in an earlier quest, but hook up the seconed accelerator to release into the larger ring, &6in the opposite direction.&r If you want, you can even build two dual-ring setups, and then have one ring release into the other ring. The particles will &5smash together, &rreleasing tachyon particles as well as creating a new item, as long as it's one of the items you CAN create with collisions."
		""
		"To complete this quest, I want you to create an &6Overcharged Crystal. &rWhile you CAN create it without a collider, don't you want to test out your sweet new tech?"
	]
	quest.4E4C0D8ECF5AA370.quest_subtitle: "It's 10."
	quest.4E4C0D8ECF5AA370.title: "It's Over 9-"
	quest.4E57613803DF3DFD.quest_subtitle: "Welcome back, SethBling here."
	quest.4E57613803DF3DFD.title: "SethBling's Apprentice"
	quest.4F0687DF51533932.quest_desc: ["This &bMachine Addon&r lets you access a specific machine slot, be it input or output. You can use it to pipe in or extract items in configurations that are &aa bit tight!&r The addon's GUI will let you select &9one&r slot the proxy will represent. You can then connect pipes or hoppers to it to extract and insert."]
	quest.4F0687DF51533932.quest_subtitle: "Let me do it for you"
	quest.4F0687DF51533932.title: "A Proxy with Moxie"
	quest.4F7E0A48FC355C66.quest_desc: [
		"You might think this &achainsaw&r would allow you to fell trees in one go, and you'd be right! Just hold &asneak&r while breaking the tree to chop the whole thing down."
		""
		"Wait, what's that? You remember this axe &odidn't&r do that? You must be crazy. It's always done that."
	]
	quest.4F7E0A48FC355C66.quest_subtitle: "VRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRR"
	quest.4F7E0A48FC355C66.title: "A Texas Massacre"
	quest.4F80A49BB0866400.quest_desc: ["This little computer chip is but a humble crafting ingredient. It's &2still important, though!"]
	quest.4F80A49BB0866400.quest_subtitle: "I synthetize and rasterize immaterial things that I fabricate for youuuuuuu"
	quest.4F80A49BB0866400.title: "I'm Your GPU"
	quest.4FD25C98B8E1E6AB.quest_desc: ["Use this quest to get &binfinite Iron Shovels!"]
	quest.4FD25C98B8E1E6AB.quest_subtitle: "Market Gardening"
	quest.4FD98EB0498E0B05.quest_subtitle: "yum"
	quest.4FD98EB0498E0B05.title: "Biologically Fueled"
	quest.4FED63E403B98023.quest_desc: [
		"Machines have a set processing speed. However, who's to say they can't work &2faster???"
		""
		"Each one of these speed upgrades will make your machine work &a10% faster, &rat the cost of &c-4% energy efficiency. &rHowever, perhaps there is &eanother addon&r which can offset this energy cost?"
		""
		"With more advanced &acores, &ryou'll be able to put more &baddons&r onto one machine. With enough speed addons, you can make your machines &aREALLY FAST!!"
	]
	quest.4FED63E403B98023.quest_subtitle: "This joke is done to DEATH"
	quest.4FED63E403B98023.title: "Gotta Go...Moderately Quick"
	quest.507FFCE1B0F87B83.quest_desc: ["In order to make this, you'll need either &6Tank 2 or Tank 3 in a Refiner.&r From there, you can use it in the Fluid Centerfuge to create Mineral Slurry!"]
	quest.507FFCE1B0F87B83.quest_subtitle: "[BUUUUURP]"
	quest.507FFCE1B0F87B83.title: "Gastric Reflux"
	quest.50EDA36D398B7132.quest_subtitle: "You don't understand. Nobody EVER jumps for the beef."
	quest.50EDA36D398B7132.title: "Parkour Civilized"
	quest.50FC0937DF1576F9.quest_desc: ["This doodad will &5automatically&r fell any tree it's directly facing, provided it has energy. The tree's drops (wood, sticks, fruit) will be placed into the saw's inventory. On its own, it's fairly useless, but perhaps later on you'll discover some &emachines&r that will help you automate lumber..."]
	quest.50FC0937DF1576F9.quest_subtitle: "Luckily, I crashed into the awaiting arms...of LUMBER"
	quest.50FC0937DF1576F9.title: "LUMBER"
	quest.51273CC87D8AD31C.quest_subtitle: "Or is it????"
	quest.51273CC87D8AD31C.title: "Metroman's Weakness"
	quest.5185854A7B7C9F87.quest_desc: ["Like I said in the Fuel Rod quest, this thing can help improve the &befficiency of your fuel rods.&r Just make sure to place it adjacent to your fuel rods to reflect the energy pulses."]
	quest.5185854A7B7C9F87.quest_subtitle: "Looks like they couldn't handle the Neutron Style"
	quest.5185854A7B7C9F87.title: "Gotta Blast!"
	quest.521B03E6CC806F44.quest_desc: ["What happens when you click a power line with a wrench?"]
	quest.521B03E6CC806F44.quest_subtitle: "WHEEEE!!!!!!!!!"
	quest.521B03E6CC806F44.title: "Zip Linin'"
	quest.5235AF95FF028683.quest_subtitle: "Ooey Gooey Kablooey!"
	quest.5235AF95FF028683.title: "Holy Moly Roly Poly Crawling in Guacamole!"
	quest.5292A1CEEAE22FC3.quest_desc: [
		"Put simply, OriTech is a &z&lwonderfully charming&r&r tech mod centered around machines that have &oamazing animations&r and &obeautifully-crafted&r deployment sequences."
		""
		"Cosmetics aside, OriTech has its own tech tree and automation equipment that can help you automate farming, mob grinding, and mining through an all-too-familiar electricity and pipe system."
		""
		"Don't be scared! This ain't &cGregTech &ror anything like that! While it may seem complex, the tech tree is actually fairly simple, and I'll be here to guide you through every step of the way."
	]
	quest.5292A1CEEAE22FC3.quest_subtitle: "What DO it do?"
	quest.5297C73BAB12CA68.quest_desc: ["This component allows you to insert &bcoolant (ice)&r into your reactor. You should place these in the &2roof&r of the reactor, above each stack of &9coolant absorbers."]
	quest.5297C73BAB12CA68.quest_subtitle: "Ice Ice Baby"
	quest.5297C73BAB12CA68.title: "Cool as Ice"
	quest.530C25EA2F19A890.quest_subtitle: "Bingle Bongle Glingle Glongle"
	quest.530C25EA2F19A890.title: "Oopy Gloopy"
	quest.532D28366814D2E6.quest_subtitle: "Fun tip: Did you know you can MAKE budding amethyst in the particle collider?"
	quest.532D28366814D2E6.title: "Budding Relations"
	quest.53C59C852D6220DD.quest_desc: [
		"&dPlutonium&r is a much more potent radioactive fuel than &aUranium&r, but it's harder to get. There are a few ways:"
		""
		"- Fire an &bEnderic Laser&r at a &aUranium Crystal Cluster.&r Note that the cluster will be destroyed, so it's not like an Amethyst Crystal. (Helpful tip: &5Silk Touch&r can be used to pick up crystal clusters.)"
		""
		"- Collide &aUranium&r and &dFluxite&r in a &eParticle Accelerator.&r You need 2500J of energy for the collision to work."
		""
		"- Obtain tiny dusts as a byproduct of processing &aRaw Uranium&r in the &6Fragment Forge."
		""
		"Of course, you can also use Plutonium for something a little more...&4explosive."
	]
	quest.53C59C852D6220DD.quest_subtitle: "Warning: Do not ingest"
	quest.53C59C852D6220DD.title: "High-Energy Pellet"
	quest.53D5F6AE5EBC2902.quest_subtitle: "GROMMIT WE'VE GOT TO LOOK FOR CHEEEEESE"
	quest.53D5F6AE5EBC2902.title: "Curse of the Were-hare"
	quest.545FB352FA893898.quest_subtitle: "Whenever you get a double-long Frosted Mini Wheat, it's officially now called a \"Mega Wheat\""
	quest.545FB352FA893898.title: "Mega Wheats"
	quest.549CE3A7DDA97C2B.quest_desc: [
		"Now this thing's the real deal! It's basically a &eplacable battery."
		""
		"Each battery has two inputs and two outputs. The &agreen plugs &rare the energy inputs, and the &cred plugs&r are the energy outputs. There's also two &bblue upgrade plugs&r which you can use to increase the battery's energy capacity, using a &9capacitor addon."
	]
	quest.549CE3A7DDA97C2B.quest_subtitle: "I couldn't think of a better quest name."
	quest.549CE3A7DDA97C2B.title: "Batter Up!"
	quest.54F239339BD33B23.quest_subtitle: "Gaben"
	quest.54F239339BD33B23.title: "Gaben"
	quest.56542F560C631D8A.quest_desc: ["For some odd reason, at this point in the game (IF you've made a Dubious Container) you can make the &5Ultra Machine core&r &obefore&r the &6Elite Machine core.&r Enjoy it, I suppose."]
	quest.56542F560C631D8A.quest_subtitle: "<Insert dripped-out Goku here>"
	quest.56542F560C631D8A.title: "Ultra Instinct Core"
	quest.5732E39B04C7742E.quest_subtitle: "There's GOLD in them there hills!"
	quest.5732E39B04C7742E.title: "49er"
	quest.57A56F75999F89D5.quest_desc: [
		"The first thing you'll need to make your particles go ZOOM is a linear motor. These thingies, when powered, will cause your particles to gain some speed every time they pass by it."
		""
		"&eNote that these motors will not increase the top speed of the particle!&r They will increase the acceleration, but you can use a &6single motor&r to get a particle to a very fast speed. It will just take a while."
	]
	quest.57A56F75999F89D5.quest_subtitle: "This takes WAY MORE than 6 D batteries"
	quest.57A56F75999F89D5.title: "Hot Wheels Booster"
	quest.57F8A26EF8EF62BB.quest_desc: ["Use this quest to get &binfinite Iron Axes!"]
	quest.57F8A26EF8EF62BB.quest_subtitle: "I must axe you a question"
	quest.580274FE55577686.quest_desc: [
		"Using your new &2dubious container&r, you can try and capture the intelligence of a small, flying magical creature. The &bAllay&r fits that description well, but when you click on it with the container, it snatches it right up! There are &ltwo&r ways to go about this:"
		""
		"-&2Give the Allay something to hold, and then use the container to suck it up"
		"-&cCapture a different type of entity. &r(What entity looks like the Allay?)"
		""
		"A rather &lvexing&r question indeed...."
		""
		"Once you have this unholy brain bottle, you can use it in place of an &5AI Chip&r in any recipe that requires it. However, I think using AI chips will be more efficient, since you don't have to go hunting around for these lil flying guys. Plus, it's more ethical!"
	]
	quest.580274FE55577686.quest_subtitle: "Is...this even ethical???"
	quest.580274FE55577686.title: "Brain in a Bottle"
	quest.58593526F6F3E97E.quest_subtitle: "Let bygones be bygones"
	quest.58593526F6F3E97E.title: "Under the Bridge"
	quest.585DF18EF9C74540.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pulverizing&r &bEnder Pearls&r will net you this mysterious slimy goop with some interesting properties. You'll be using it to make the &3Enderic Laser, &ra machine necessary for progression."
		""
		"What's that? You're playing on &2peaceful mode?&r Well, the way I see it, there's two ways to go about it:"
		""
		"- &6Purchase&r some Pearls from the shop"
		""
		"- Use some &3Sculk.&r But how to get some? You'll need a &5Silk Touch&r tool..."
	]
	quest.585DF18EF9C74540.quest_subtitle: "Jamaco!"
	quest.585DF18EF9C74540.title: "World of Goo"
	quest.5884535D762F1348.quest_subtitle: "heh. hee hee. BAHAHAHAHAHAHA"
	quest.5884535D762F1348.title: "Boner Donor"
	quest.595017C3A21CC480.quest_desc: [
		"Use Fluid pipes to route that new Steam into this device, and it'll start going to work generating delicious &eElectricity!&r However, it also generates a bit of &9water&r overtime as well, and if the tank gets full, then it won't generate any more electricity until it's emptied. Luckily, I've provided a &5Fluid-voiding trashcan&r for you to use, and you can always craft more fluid voids as well."
		""
		"Oh, and did you know you can &2chain&r these generators together? They'll share steam inputs and water/electricity outputs, so you only need pipes going from one of them."
	]
	quest.595017C3A21CC480.quest_subtitle: "They're two, they're four, they're six, they're eight"
	quest.595017C3A21CC480.title: "Really Useful Engines"
	quest.5A327FD28AE28058.quest_subtitle: "It's like \"Flesh Target.\" What? I'd like to see YOU do better!"
	quest.5A327FD28AE28058.title: "Flarget"
	quest.5A44CC49C896C907.quest_desc: ["This bad boy will emit a beam of high-energy particles wherever you click! This beam can damage entities, transfer energy, and mine blocks. &4However, the \"mine blocks\" part doesn't seem to work right based on my testing.&r"]
	quest.5A44CC49C896C907.quest_subtitle: "A Nitrome Classic"
	quest.5A44CC49C896C907.title: "Off the Rails"
	quest.5C13D71D97C7B4FA.quest_desc: [
		"A little later on in this modpack, you'll encounter &dDrones, &rwhich are capable of bulk transporting a lot of items very quickly. However, when it comes to personal transit, I've taken the liberty of including this handy &5Teleporter Mod.&r"
		""
		"Using the teleporter is quite simple. You'll need an &bEnder Shard&r and a &5Teleporter&r (for a one-way trip. You need another set for a round trip, obvi.) While holding the Ender Shard, &6Shift-click&r the spot you want to teleport the player. Then, all you have to do is pop the Ender Shard inside of the Teleporter. &aSneak while standing on the Teleporter&r to zip to the spot you marked earlier!"
		""
		"I'll throw you one &9Teleporter Set &rfor free. Try not to lose it!!!"
		""
		"Oh, and you can use &zEnhanced Ender Shards&r for cross-dimensional travel."
	]
	quest.5C13D71D97C7B4FA.quest_subtitle: "Thanks for the ride, pardner."
	quest.5C13D71D97C7B4FA.title: "Teleporter, Goin' Up!"
	quest.5C3B5EDC6EE0F1B8.quest_desc: [
		"So many addons...and not enough space..."
		""
		"The Splicer allows you to merge addons together into a single, powerful &z\"Heart of the Machine\"&r addon."
		""
		"You'll need a &eLOT of power&r to do the merge, which will get consumed all at once upon clicking the merge button. To merge addons, just connect them all to the back of the machine using Addon Extenders, like you would with a normal machine. &cThe extenders will get consumed in the merge&r, so make sure to say your goodbyes."
		""
		"Oh, and a couple things about the Heart of the Machine addon:"
		""
		"- You cannot merge this addon with more addons. So make sure you are absolutely sure about the addons you WANT to merge."
		""
		"- The Heart of the Machine is incompatible with other addons once added to a machine. It must be the first AND ONLY addon attached."
		""
		"- You cannot get the addons back once you've merged them."
	]
	quest.5C3B5EDC6EE0F1B8.quest_subtitle: "Who invited the Rapture?"
	quest.5C3B5EDC6EE0F1B8.title: "Biologically Shocking!"
	quest.5C81699081D18DA2.quest_desc: ["&4DANGER!!!! This device will EXPLODE IMMEDIATELY after being activated. Please assure you are a suitable distance away from it before activating!!!"]
	quest.5C81699081D18DA2.quest_subtitle: "TACTICAL NUKE, INCOMING!!!"
	quest.5C81699081D18DA2.title: "25 Kills"
	quest.5DC3BFF2305B2F1D.quest_desc: ["By alloying &eNickel &rand &dFluxite&r together, you'll get this mysterious glowing ingot. It can be used to make a couple of Machine Addons, but its main use is probably the creation of &bSuperconductors."]
	quest.5DC3BFF2305B2F1D.quest_subtitle: "I am going to turn into a truck now"
	quest.5DC3BFF2305B2F1D.title: "Cybertronian Snack"
	quest.5E9234E7C066F868.quest_subtitle: "True as it can be"
	quest.5E9234E7C066F868.title: "Tale as old as time"
	quest.5FE982DA625B09D7.quest_desc: [
		"This is it: The &aheart and soul&r of your nuclear reactor. There is also a &6double and quadruple&r version of the fuel rod, which will consume more fuel and generate more heat, but will also output more power."
		""
		"Fuel rods will also emit &apulses of energy&r which, when they hit other adjacent fuel rods, will provide additional power. You can also use &bNeutron Reflectors&r to reflect these pulses back onto fuel rods to increase their efficiency and power output."
	]
	quest.5FE982DA625B09D7.quest_subtitle: "Smokin' Hot Uranium babes want to date YOU!!!"
	quest.5FE982DA625B09D7.title: "Hot Singles in Your Area"
	quest.6009C1B3FABA448F.quest_desc: ["Compared to mods like GregTech and Immersive Engineering, OriTech's steel is mercifully simple to create. All you need is to combine &9iron and coal&r in a crafting table. This will give you steel at a 2:1 ratio, though there will soon be other ways to craft steel that are both more efficient and renewable."]
	quest.6009C1B3FABA448F.quest_subtitle: "This was a triumph"
	quest.6009C1B3FABA448F.title: "Steel Alive"
	quest.602A4E16B7A40F36.quest_desc: [
		"This is the actual &6interface part&r of the particle accelerator. You need to place it such that the little sticky-outy-bits are around a &bparticle accelerator guide piece."
		""
		"You don't need to power this component. It is here that you'll insert items to accelerate, as well as collect the byproducts of any collision, and view stats of the latest accelerated particle."
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		"Psst...down here! Supposedly, if you collide &6fire charges&r with each other fast enough, you'll &4bring the Nether closer.&r Doing the same with &3Ender Pearls&r will bring the End closer. And somehow...through SOME mean...there MIGHT be a way to create..."
		""
		""
		""
		"&0A Black Hole."
	]
	quest.602A4E16B7A40F36.quest_subtitle: "Mooom! Phineas and Ferb are creating new and exotic forms of matter as well as countless tachyons!!!"
	quest.602A4E16B7A40F36.title: "I Have A Few ConCERNs"
	quest.6078DC9CF5886782.quest_subtitle: "Aren't GUNS supposed to be ILLEGAL, Mojang?"
	quest.6078DC9CF5886782.title: "Gunpowder General Store"
	quest.60A44B7E06B5DF75.quest_subtitle: "Because I'm a POTATO"
	quest.60A44B7E06B5DF75.title: "So, How Are You Holding Up?"
	quest.60A964E1E24CD447.quest_desc: [
		"Centrifuging your new sheet of Biopolymer (with some water) will create a nice sheet of plastic! This is a very useful crafting ingredient, and it also has a neat block form for easy storage."
		""
		"Oh, what's that? Another recipe? Well, I suppose you can turn Sand and &8Crude Oil&r into Polymer Resin, and then centrifuge that...but I think the biopolymer route is the easier way to go."
	]
	quest.60A964E1E24CD447.quest_subtitle: "Life in Plastic, it's Fantastic"
	quest.60A964E1E24CD447.title: "I'm a Barbie Girl"
	quest.6109176C6F174BF3.quest_subtitle: "I like you.................................as a friend."
	quest.6109176C6F174BF3.title: "Plat-onic Relationship"
	quest.6150374563F888B5.quest_desc: [
		"Of course, what would a modpack be without a &agood set of goals to accomplish?"
		""
		"By checkmarking this quest, you'll reveal the &lAutomation Challenges &rchapter, which grants access to a plethora of challenges where you have to sink &6hundreds, &ethousands, &ror even &4MILLIONS &rof items to complete them!"
		""
		"You'll also get a &lTask Screen, &rwhich you can use to sink items into to complete these quests. Items WILL be consumed, but that's why there's automation!"
		""
		"You can &afinally break Task Screens with your fists, now.&r So if you want more task screens, then you can craft some more using Stone and Books."
	]
	quest.6150374563F888B5.quest_subtitle: "You pass butter"
	quest.6190B225EC5005D2.quest_desc: ["This is like a much &2better&r version of the &aSpeed Addon.&r It gives more speed, &oAND&r it also gives an &2energy efficiency boost&r!!"]
	quest.6190B225EC5005D2.quest_subtitle: "I'm gonna need that quarterly report on my desk by Monday, mmmmmkay?"
	quest.6190B225EC5005D2.title: "Synergize Your Workflows"
	quest.61924FA0B1A6134C.quest_subtitle: "It's Wabbit season"
	quest.61924FA0B1A6134C.title: "Eh, What's Up, Doc?"
	quest.61F434988424BB45.quest_subtitle: "I don't know what this is, I'll mine it anyways"
	quest.61F434988424BB45.title: "Mining Away"
	quest.62B3FE1A0C93C339.quest_subtitle: "25 25 25 do I hear 30 25 25 25 30 do I hear 40"
	quest.62B3FE1A0C93C339.title: "E(nder)Bay"
	quest.62C693EC4BBF2095.quest_desc: [
		"The goal of this modpack is to teach you, &zthe player&r, about OriTech. However, the regular old Minecraft Grind might be a little bit discouraging to some. Thus, I've generously provided some quests that will provide an &bunlimited source of three iron tools&r for you to exploit as much as you want. Wait, why not &3Diamond tools?&r Well, I want you to be encouraged to make the &6Hand Drill and Chainsaw, that's why."
		""
		"Additionally, this quest will provide a modest stack of food for you to eat. If you're playing on &cpeaceful mode,&r this will &estill be useful!!!&r That's right, hunger has now been enabled in peaceful. This is to encourage you to create automated farms and things like that."
	]
	quest.62C693EC4BBF2095.quest_subtitle: "Nose to the grindstone!!! *Proceeds to disenchant nose*"
	quest.62D0B7DC79A3C046.quest_desc: [
		"Your first &lgenerator!&r Generators will be used to generate Electrical Power, which is crucial for energizing machines. This generator takes &6combustable fuels&r (anything that can be used to fuel a furnace is fair game, with a few exceptions) and outputs a steady stream of electricity."
		""
		"One helpful thing to know: A generator will only make progress towards &cconsuming fuel&r if energy is being used. So, you don't have to worry about &cwasting resources&r if your machines are idle."
	]
	quest.62D0B7DC79A3C046.quest_subtitle: "L'dor Vador"
	quest.62D0B7DC79A3C046.title: "From Generation to Generation"
	quest.62FDE8D8166EC051.quest_desc: ["Through some kind of &5divine magic &r(or it could be the bouncy silicon/silicone bottoms), these boots will negate &4all fall damage. &rYes, I do mean &4ALL."]
	quest.62FDE8D8166EC051.quest_subtitle: "Cave Johnson here. We designed these puppies to protect the sensitive and expensive equipment in your inventory. Your health and safety just so happens to be a happy byproduct."
	quest.62FDE8D8166EC051.title: "Long Fall Boots"
	quest.630B2CC551D7DDEC.quest_subtitle: "Bad to the bone"
	quest.630B2CC551D7DDEC.title: "The Bone Zone"
	quest.6357F1D5EE8C1324.quest_desc: ["There's a clump for every season! Well, not really. But there IS a clump for every &6metal ore.&r Get one of each to complete this quest."]
	quest.6357F1D5EE8C1324.quest_subtitle: "Stick together!"
	quest.6357F1D5EE8C1324.title: "Clumping Along"
	quest.637062E61797BC8A.quest_desc: [
		"For the most part, this pack can be played completely normally in &6peaceful mode. &rHowever, access to certain items (bones, gunpowder, etc) gets blocked off due to hostile mobs not spawning."
		""
		"Normally, this wouldn't be a problem, but &bender pearls &rend up being &ocrucial &rto progression. Thus, checkmarking this quest unlocks a mini shop of sorts, where you can manually sell any excess metals for these drops. You can also substitute &3sculk&r for ender pearls when making &5enderic compound&r (the so-called \"crucial progression item\") if you're not in the shopping mood. However, you'll need &5silk touch &rto get it..."
	]
	quest.637062E61797BC8A.quest_subtitle: "Peace out, brah!"
	quest.637546B4D70E38AA.quest_desc: [
		"Another material you can make once you have a &6Pulverizer &ris Biomass. It's made by pulverizing organic things, like food and seeds. If you've got a farm going, this would be a good place to send excess seeds."
		""
		"&aBiomass &ris the first step towards two important things: &5Renewable power, &rand &7Plastic."
	]
	quest.637546B4D70E38AA.quest_subtitle: "Yummy!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
	quest.637546B4D70E38AA.title: "Plant Goop"
	quest.63B5604A22F1CEC5.quest_subtitle: "Who the heck is \"Nick-le?\""
	quest.63B5604A22F1CEC5.title: "Nickle Ingot"
	quest.6433E94494554D84.quest_desc: ["This component allows you to extract the energy produced by the Nuclear Reactor. It's probably wise to put it on the &asides&r of the reactor."]
	quest.6433E94494554D84.quest_subtitle: "All ashore that's going ashore!"
	quest.6433E94494554D84.title: "Port of Call"
	quest.64C977584430F1B5.quest_subtitle: "PERRY THE PLATINUM?????"
	quest.64C977584430F1B5.title: "A Plat-ypus?"
	quest.64D0ACDCB11A6699.quest_desc: [
		"These tough walls will form the frame of your reactor. Ideally, you should build a &6rectangular or cubic frame&r with a solid bottom, top, and walls. You can then bust holes in the walls and roof of the reactor to put in ports for fuel, energy, and coolant."
		""
		"Inside the frame will be your &afuel rods&r, &eheat distribution&r, &9cooling&r, and &bneutron deflectors&r. You can actually build just one layer, and then duplicate that layout as high as you want your reactor to be. Experiment with different configurations to get &5maximum efficiency&r!"
	]
	quest.64D0ACDCB11A6699.quest_subtitle: "HEY! Teachers! Leave us kids alone!"
	quest.64D0ACDCB11A6699.title: "Another Brick in the Wall"
	quest.652FABF8C35110D9.quest_desc: [
		"This high-tech engraving machine is capable of producing &5advanced&r computer chips, as well as doing other recipes. However, it has one quirk: &cIt can't be powered by Energy Pipes!"
		""
		"So how do you power it, then? Well, you have to use your &bEnderic Lasers!&r Use your Targeting Device to select the center of the Forge, and then set a Laser to point towards it. It will begin transferring energy wirelessly to the forge, provided you've plugged in the laser, of course."
	]
	quest.652FABF8C35110D9.quest_subtitle: "We're on the etch of disaster!"
	quest.652FABF8C35110D9.title: "Engrave Danger"
	quest.65850F392A0F8BF6.quest_desc: [
		"This is the axe you've been axe-ing for. It is capable of &dfelling entire trees in one go!&r All you have to do is hold shift while breaking a log, and then shout \"TIMBERRRRR!!!!*\""
		""
		"Oh, it's also &aunbreakable."
		""
		"*Note: Shouting \"TIMBERRRR\" is not actually required. However, you're free to do so, as long as you don't mind your roommates/parents thinking you're a &oweirdo."
	]
	quest.65850F392A0F8BF6.quest_subtitle: "Finally...ULTIMATE LUMBER"
	quest.65850F392A0F8BF6.title: "Treecapitation"
	quest.6588F5527F91CE64.quest_desc: [
		"This addon allows for \"Burst Processing.\" Basically, the machine will operate MUCH, MUCH faster! But...if the machine operates for too long, the processor will overheat and the machine will be throttled. You'll need to let the machine cool down before you can operate unthrottled again."
		""
		"Chaining more burst processors will let you Burst Process for longer!"
	]
	quest.6588F5527F91CE64.quest_subtitle: "Lord have mercy I'm gonna BUUUUU-"
	quest.6588F5527F91CE64.title: "Burst Processing"
	quest.665BECF0C3AAFB6F.quest_subtitle: "I'm gonna step on the gas"
	quest.665BECF0C3AAFB6F.title: "Gas Gas Gas"
	quest.66975E795271ADF9.quest_desc: [
		"Finding ore is &4HARD."
		""
		"Let's make it &aa little easier."
		""
		"The Advanced Finders mod brings you &5three special compasses&r that will point in the direction of the nearest ore. The little hands will move to point at the nearest ore deposit. You might also see some &aarrows&r, which indicates vertically up/down."
		""
		"Oh, and for some reason, you can convert the finder into a &6different type&r by right-clicking with it in hand. It's a bit finicky, though, so I'll just give you 1 of each. What can I saaaay except...you're welcome!"
	]
	quest.66975E795271ADF9.quest_subtitle: "Losers weepers"
	quest.66975E795271ADF9.title: "Finders Keepers"
	quest.67FEF3B6E5F3A35F.quest_desc: ["This component is one of two methods of &6cooling off your reactor.&r This is the passive method of cooling, which means it doesn't need any sort of coolant, but it's the &cless efficient method.&r Don't forget to connect your heat pipes from the fuel rods to the vents!"]
	quest.67FEF3B6E5F3A35F.quest_subtitle: "There is an impostor Among Us"
	quest.67FEF3B6E5F3A35F.title: "Sussy Wussy"
	quest.68556EDD5B9B169F.quest_desc: ["Use this quest to get &binfinite Iron Pickaxes!"]
	quest.68556EDD5B9B169F.quest_subtitle: "Diggy Diggy Hole"
	quest.692FA3619F21E912.quest_subtitle: "I like my steaks drippy bruh"
	quest.692FA3619F21E912.title: "Medium Rare"
	quest.693CBDDB2F05CF4E.quest_desc: ["Motors are a crafting component used in a wide variety of machines. They use a special &emagnetic coil &rcrafted using your newfound steel, as well as some nickel. You should have crafted a couple when you made your basic generator. Once you have motors, you've basically won the game. Yeah. True story."]
	quest.693CBDDB2F05CF4E.quest_subtitle: "Only on Disney XD!"
	quest.693CBDDB2F05CF4E.title: "MotorCity"
	quest.6945CA940CB01C20.quest_desc: ["The Solar Panel is a very useful source of energy, because it uses &ethe sun!&r It will produce energy as long as the sun is out, and fold up at night. Remember, &6better cores&r will increase &aenergy production!"]
	quest.6945CA940CB01C20.quest_subtitle: "SOLAR!"
	quest.6945CA940CB01C20.title: "Get THAT Through Your System"
	quest.6A2F4174F0E45088.quest_subtitle: "Why so sad?"
	quest.6A2F4174F0E45088.title: "Feeling Blue"
	quest.6AAEE689B6215B28.quest_subtitle: "Or H20MG, AKA Water + Magnesium"
	quest.6AAEE689B6215B28.title: "H20h My God"
	quest.6AAF4B14EDCCD0CE.quest_subtitle: "Error: Too Much Wood"
	quest.6AAF4B14EDCCD0CE.title: "Crash Log"
	quest.6AD33D71E5683D02.quest_subtitle: "Doo doo doo DOO!"
	quest.6AD33D71E5683D02.title: "Intel Inside"
	quest.6B5FCFBCBA2A9956.quest_subtitle: "Think of how many torches you could have made!"
	quest.6B5FCFBCBA2A9956.title: "Non Renewable"
	quest.6B7B4AAE00327C0D.quest_desc: ["When particles collide, they release tons and tons of &etachyons.&r With these high-tech energy absorbers, you can take these tachyons and convert them into energy. With the right configuration (make sure to thoroughly surround the collision area with absorbers), you can make up to &etriple the energy&r you use to initially accelerate the particles!"]
	quest.6B7B4AAE00327C0D.quest_subtitle: "Best Friends Whenever"
	quest.6B7B4AAE00327C0D.title: "I'm Fast as Frick, Boi"
	quest.6B9A1057D3138BE1.quest_subtitle: "Rated H for Hydrocarbon"
	quest.6B9A1057D3138BE1.title: "Crude Humor"
	quest.6BB87C5892CE7F9B.quest_desc: ["Item Pipes aren't the only thing-mover-arounder in this mod. There's also &9Fluid Pipes, &rwhich can move liquids around. They work VERY similarly to item pipes, in that you can &6click on them&r to tell them to extract from whatever container they're attached to. You can also use the &epipe wrench &rto get rid of unwanted connections, just like in a lot of other mods."]
	quest.6BB87C5892CE7F9B.quest_subtitle: "Dunna dunna dunna"
	quest.6BB87C5892CE7F9B.title: "World 1-2"
	quest.6C5FA4D6EE53931B.quest_subtitle: "Tag a friend to immediately receive 8000 Roentgens of radiation!!!!"
	quest.6C5FA4D6EE53931B.title: "Elephant Foot Friday"
	quest.6CA25970FBFE71F6.quest_desc: [
		"This magical cage of black magic allows you to &5spawn nearly any mob in the game.&r Yes, this does include the &8Wither.&r You'll also need &aCages, &rthe amount of which depends on the size of the mob you capture. The first mob to walk over the cage will get &6captured.&r From there, you'll need to use the Cages to build a suitable-sized cage to spawn the mob. By clicking the spawner, you'll see the size of the cage you need to build."
		""
		"Once the cage is built, you'll need to feed &5souls&r into the spawner. Once this condition is met (bigger mobs need more souls), mobs will start to spawn from the cage. Since it costs souls to generate mobs, you might want to start a &9Soul Flower farm."
	]
	quest.6CA25970FBFE71F6.quest_subtitle: "EIEIOh my god this is black magic isn't it?"
	quest.6CA25970FBFE71F6.title: "Old McDonald"
	quest.6CA3103473145B68.quest_subtitle: "Da ba dee da ba die"
	quest.6CA3103473145B68.title: "I'm Blue"
	quest.6CD36149A1A12CDF.quest_subtitle: "Here's to the first female computer programmer!"
	quest.6CD36149A1A12CDF.title: "Lovelace Architecture"
	quest.6D2E5C56D9A976E4.quest_desc: [
		"This is the &5Ultimate Pickaxe.&r By shift-right clicking, you can switch between Silk Touch mode and Area Effect mode."
		""
		"It's also UNBREAKABLE, and has the fastest mining speed in the game. It basically &ainsta-mines&r dirt, and it ain't no slacker when it comes to deepslate, either. Use the area-effect mode to drill tunnels, and the silk touch mode to collect ores so you can &bdouble them&r in the Fragment Forge."
	]
	quest.6D2E5C56D9A976E4.quest_subtitle: "It's mine all mine"
	quest.6D2E5C56D9A976E4.title: "Pick Your Battles"
	quest.6D3DF08898C4676F.quest_desc: [
		"Combining some Silicon Wafers (presumably they are unengraved) with a &1Processer&r forms an &6advanced computing engine!&r"
		""
		"Real-life fun fact: Being \"Turing Complete\" means that something can, theoretically, simulate any computer program in existence, assuming you have infinite time and memory. &6Minecraft is technically Turing Complete!"
	]
	quest.6D3DF08898C4676F.quest_subtitle: "But can it run Minecraft?"
	quest.6D3DF08898C4676F.title: "Turing Complete"
	quest.6D6B2E5919EC7BCA.quest_desc: ["This is the final, and most &dpowerful&r Research Addon. Affix it to the side of your Research Center to unlock the final level of Upgrades."]
	quest.6D6B2E5919EC7BCA.quest_subtitle: "A League...of Legends"
	quest.6D6B2E5919EC7BCA.title: "We're Gonna Need a League"
	quest.6DBD6854042DC363.quest_subtitle: "Only shooting stars break the mold"
	quest.6DBD6854042DC363.title: "All That Glitters"
	quest.6E0A5FB2DA943CB9.quest_subtitle: "Chewing through shaders in no time flat!"
	quest.6E0A5FB2DA943CB9.title: "Blast Processing"
	quest.6E365B38C053B008.quest_subtitle: "How bad could this POSSIBLY be?"
	quest.6E365B38C053B008.title: "The Once-Ler"
	quest.6EDD0C0E459BCCE4.quest_desc: [
		"&5Enchantments&r can upgrade your tools, so why not upgrade &oyourself?"
		""
		"This Cybernetic Enhancement Station can imbue your person with fantastic abilities, for a hefty material fee, of course."
		""
		"Once you build the structure, you can &2walk inside&r to bring up the upgrades menu. Of course, without any &bResearch Addons, &ryou can't actually research anything yet..."
		""
		"...but once you do get some &dresearch addons&r, you'll need to provide power and the research materials to the center. Once you unlock a research item, you can apply and remove that addon at will (useful for some addons that change the size of the player!). Some addons are toggleable using &2a wheel menu, accesible by holding down \"G\"."
	]
	quest.6EDD0C0E459BCCE4.quest_subtitle: "In 2077, what makes someone a criminal? Getting cock-"
	quest.6EDD0C0E459BCCE4.title: "Cyber Punked"
	quest.6F88217A13591F0F.quest_subtitle: "Made in a proper copper coffee pot"
	quest.6F88217A13591F0F.title: "All I Want is a Proper Cup of Coffee"
	quest.6FAF8D7D7501F262.quest_desc: [
		"With Biosteel in hand, you can create another multiblock generator: the &2Bio Generator. &rIt comsumes organic fuel, such as seeds, wheat, or even those &epacked wheat or &4solid biofuel &rcake things you made."
		""
		"&4DANGER: This generator makes a REALLY WEIRD uncomfortable squishing/squelching sound. It has no impact on gameplay. However, it is REALLY, REALLY, gross."
	]
	quest.6FAF8D7D7501F262.quest_subtitle: "The noise this generator makes is absolutely horrible and whoever chose the sound for it should feel really bad about themselves."
	quest.6FAF8D7D7501F262.title: "The Generator That Makes A Really Horrible Squishy Noise"
	quest.715A3825715BA814.quest_subtitle: "HEADBANG! HEADBANG! HEADBANG!"
	quest.715A3825715BA814.title: "Metallica"
	quest.717E87A10CD6EFE6.quest_desc: ["Sheol Fire can be used in the &6Lava Generator for power&r, and it can also be used in the Refinery with any Raw Metal to both turn that metal into clumps, &6and create Lava at the same time.&r"]
	quest.717E87A10CD6EFE6.quest_subtitle: ":)"
	quest.717E87A10CD6EFE6.title: "Fire In The Hole!!!"
	quest.71830898EE161436.quest_desc: [
		"This component is arguably the most &6important &rin your accelerator, so pay attention!"
		""
		"These guides will form the basis for the closed circuit of your accelerator. Right-clicking the guide will bend the glass part 45 degrees. Use these to make the particle turn corners to form a closed loop. You can also use them as straight guides to make slower particles go across larger gaps. Applying a &credstone signal&r will allow you to switch it between straight and bent, so you can release the particles &eautomatically."
		""
		"Wait, what was that about \"larger gaps?\""
		""
		"You see, particles have a &5maximum gap length&r and a &dminimum curve radius.&r As particles speed up, they can travel for &alonger distances&r without needing to hit a guide piece. However, the faster they travel, the &cwider curve&r they have to take, otherwise they will &9fly out of the ring!"
		""
		"The optimal strategy is to have a smaller starting ring that gets the particle up to a decent speed, and then have a system that automatically releases the particle into a larger ring to further accelerate the particle."
	]
	quest.71830898EE161436.quest_subtitle: "To the other siiiiide..."
	quest.71830898EE161436.title: "I'll Be Your Guide"
	quest.71A40BD6A864D491.quest_subtitle: "I'm famished"
	quest.71A40BD6A864D491.title: "Ireland's Hero"
	quest.72CE8244C0BD1C3A.quest_desc: ["This addon will give an attached machine some &badditional energy capacity,&r but it can also be used as a place to extract or insert energy. Useful for weird, compact setups."]
	quest.72CE8244C0BD1C3A.quest_subtitle: "Power from another source"
	quest.72CE8244C0BD1C3A.title: "Surge Protector"
	quest.7340072E067A6DDF.quest_desc: ["You did it! This is the &eLast tier of ingot&r in this mod. With it, you can create incredibly powerful tools, and the highest and last tier of Machine core."]
	quest.7340072E067A6DDF.quest_subtitle: "No horrific eagle punishment necessary!"
	quest.7340072E067A6DDF.title: "The Gift of Fire"
	quest.734BB48B330DABC1.quest_desc: [
		"If you've been skilled enough to fight the &cWither, &rthen you might have gotten your hands on some &5Wither Roses.&r (which are obtained when a wither kills a mob near a flower). These wither roses can be used to craft &9Soul Seeds&r, which are grown on Soul Soil. When fully grown, breaking them will release a &bSoul&r (as well as some more seeds!), which will fly towards the nearest machine which uses souls."
		""
		"Oh, and if you're playing on &apeaceful...&rmaybe there's something in the &6shop&r that can help you get a Wither rose?"
	]
	quest.734BB48B330DABC1.quest_subtitle: "But where did the souls come from???"
	quest.734BB48B330DABC1.title: "Soul Seeds"
	quest.7368270A1F6C6CB9.quest_desc: [
		"The &6crafter &ris, surprisingly, a &5Vanilla Minecraft addition. &rHowever, it will be pretty useful on your automation journey, so let me teach you how to use it."
		""
		"In the crafter's interface, you can click on a slot to enable/disable it. This allows you to sort of \"pigeonhole\" the items into taking on a certain shape. When items are placed into the correct shape (a crafting recipe), you can apply a &4redstone signal&r to the crafter to automatically craft the item!"
		""
		"This on its own is useful for single-block-type recipes (like compacted wheat), but for more complex recipes you might run into trouble trying to get the items into the right places. &2For this, you might want to look at some Youtube tutorials. &rBest of luck!"
	]
	quest.7368270A1F6C6CB9.quest_subtitle: "Vanilla's GREATEST addition"
	quest.7368270A1F6C6CB9.title: "Arts N' Crafts"
	quest.7402C647C3F54270.quest_subtitle: "You BETTER not have been submitting CHOCOLATE ingots to these quests!"
	quest.7402C647C3F54270.title: "Hanukkah Gelt"
	quest.741E0ABF3166B3BC.quest_desc: ["Alloying a sheet of Biopolymer with an iron ingot (in the foundry, remember?) will create an ingot of &2Biosteel,&r however that works. For all intents and purposes, Biosteel can be used in any recipe that needs &8regular steel.&r Additionally, there are a couple of recipes that use &5exclusively Biosteel, &rwhich is why I had you make some :)"]
	quest.741E0ABF3166B3BC.quest_subtitle: "It's like green steel, get it? No? Well F-"
	quest.741E0ABF3166B3BC.title: "Greel"
	quest.743761C14BB68540.quest_desc: [
		"The Centrifuge is another one of your early-game machines. It spins REALLY FAST to separate compounds from each other. It can separate metal clumps into &6gems&r, but you'll need a later machine to actually get those clumps."
		""
		"Instead, you'll be using this centrifuge to make &2Biopolymer&r, which is essential to making further materials."
		""
		"The Centrifuge is one of your first forays into &5multiblock machines.&r Remember how those work? Better cores = better machine performance!"
	]
	quest.743761C14BB68540.quest_subtitle: "I'm gonna puke..."
	quest.743761C14BB68540.title: "Round and Round"
	quest.7448EB9F57FBB17A.quest_desc: [
		"Under normal use, your machines will consume &eenergy. &rToo much usage will put strain on your energy network, and you might not have &cenough to go around! &rTo mitigate this, you could always &ebuild more generators...&r or you can make your machines consume less energy!"
		""
		"Each Efficiency Addon will make your machine consume &a10% less energy. &rThis is GREAT for offsetting the &cincreased energy cost&r caused by using &2speed addons."
	]
	quest.7448EB9F57FBB17A.quest_subtitle: "\"Dude, how are we going to build a pyramid with a freaking SPHERE? We ordered CUBES for a REASON!!!"
	quest.7448EB9F57FBB17A.title: "Work Smarter, Not Harder"
	quest.74BF23AE88673ED2.quest_desc: ["This cool cat can perform a couple of recipes that may or may not be useful. It can chill &8steam&r into snow, and &9water&r into &bice."]
	quest.74BF23AE88673ED2.quest_subtitle: "Nobody's gonna save you from the ice cubes of the night"
	quest.74BF23AE88673ED2.title: "Chiller Night"
	quest.75A3A8F41E4C85DF.quest_desc: [
		"Sometimes, you might have to route pipes around some very tight, tricky places. For this, we've got &6ducts!&r Ducts work just like regular pipes, but they &cwon't&r connect to machines. This means you can place them directly next to them without them accidentally pushing or pulling from them."
		""
		"In addition to item pipe ducts, there are also duct versions of &6fluid pipes, &4energy pipes, &band superconductors."
	]
	quest.75A3A8F41E4C85DF.quest_subtitle: "Sussin' around in the ducts"
	quest.75A3A8F41E4C85DF.title: "Duct Duct Goose"
	quest.75B59EB89293EC1C.quest_desc: ["Heavy Oil is refined from regular, extracted Oil using the refinery. From there, you can continue to refine it into further compounds, or you can burn it in the Fuel Generator for power."]
	quest.76A2E28C931A9757.quest_desc: [
		"This lil pumpjack can pump liquids &afrom the world&r into fluid pipes, provided you give it energy. There are a few quirks to consider:"
		""
		"- &9Water&r is infinite. Placing a pump over a single water block will pump that water infinitely. Forever."
		"- &6Lava&r is &cnot infinite. &rPlacing a pump over lava will physically remove the lava from the world. The nether certainly has a lot of lava ripe for the taking, but perhaps there is another way to get &5renewable lava?"
		"- If the pump runs out of liquid below it, you will have to &ebreak and re-place the pump&r for it to recognize new liquid. Sorry, it's just a quirk of the mod."
		"- Don't forget to right-click the connected fluid pipe to activate &6the pipe's extractor!"
	]
	quest.76A2E28C931A9757.quest_subtitle: "LOUDER!!!!"
	quest.76A2E28C931A9757.title: "Pump It!"
	quest.76DA3024F6BF09A0.quest_desc: [
		"As part of the introductory quests, you should have gotten your hands on a &6task screen."
		""
		"The Task Screen is an important block which you can use to automatically submit items towards a quest. To use it, just place it in the world, and click on it to open the menu. From here, you can set a few properties (you can give it the appearance of a block to make it blend in, etc), but what we're really looking for is &9Task. &rClick on that, and from there you can select any one of these automation quests to submit items towards."
		""
		"After you have configured the screen to accept items for a quest, you can use a hopper or item pipe to insert items into the screen. They will &5automatically be consumed,&r so make sure you REALLY want to submit them first!"
	]
	quest.76DA3024F6BF09A0.quest_subtitle: "Do it...or else."
	quest.76DA3024F6BF09A0.title: "TaskMaster"
	quest.77A40F25484F2776.quest_subtitle: "This isn't an escape vehicle! It's a pile of metal!!!"
	quest.77A40F25484F2776.title: "Get to the Copper!"
	quest.781D324AC67B58D5.quest_desc: [
		"These are basically long-distance &ePower Pylons!&r They sit quite nicely on top of the &7Industrial Support Beam&r decorative block, and require two cores each to create."
		""
		"Once you have two of them built, you must place them at least 50 blocks and no more than 1000 blocks away from each other. Then, use your &cTarget Designator&r to Shift-click on each power pole, which will link them together (with a nice little cable!)"
		""
		"Like all power equipment, &aGreen is input&r and &4Red is output."
	]
	quest.781D324AC67B58D5.quest_subtitle: "Love is Electrifying!"
	quest.781D324AC67B58D5.title: "Long-Distance Relationship"
	quest.786D572333ADC721.quest_subtitle: "Hrrr. Hrm? Hurm hurm!"
	quest.786D572333ADC721.title: "Hrm."
	quest.78AD6833C86CF758.quest_desc: [
		"Remember how I said you'd soon be discovering a way to make metals/alloys more efficiently? Well, &ahere it is!"
		""
		"The Foundry will create any of OriCraft's ingots at a 1:1 ratio as opposed to the 2:1 ratio of the crafting table. With this machine, you'll be able to create twice the amount of steel, electrum, and soon to be other mysterious metals."
	]
	quest.78AD6833C86CF758.quest_subtitle: "An alloyance? I've got to join!"
	quest.78AD6833C86CF758.title: "You can be in my alloy!"
	quest.79BFB18049E974E4.quest_desc: [
		"Using this bad boy on an &bEnderic Laser&r will allow it to target mobs. It has a range of 4 blocks, and has 3 modes. By shift-clicking the bottom of the enderic laser with your &atargeter device, &ryou can cycle through all three targeting modes."
		""
		"-&4Hostile Only"
		""
		"-&eHostile and Neutral Only"
		""
		"-&aNon-player Only"
		""
		"Combined with the Crop Filter addon, you can make it not target baby animals, so you can fully automate your livestock farms."
	]
	quest.79BFB18049E974E4.quest_subtitle: "The world's most secure password"
	quest.79BFB18049E974E4.title: "Hunter2"
	quest.79EF5A97B370125D.quest_desc: [
		"Once you've found Uranium (and have the Atomic Forge to make Uranium Gems), you can manufacture &aUranium Pellets.&r While these won't really be useful until you have a &4Nuclear Reactor, &ryou can still use them to make something...&edestructive."
		""
		"1 large pellet can also be crafted into &a9 small pellets.&r This might be useful later on when you actually get a reactor set up."
	]
	quest.79EF5A97B370125D.quest_subtitle: "Don't eat it, though."
	quest.79EF5A97B370125D.title: "ACTUAL Yellow Cake"
	quest.7AAA9B58C5C9FBFC.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have Biomass, you can use your newfound &5Assembler&r to compact it into a little brick of Biofuel. This Biofuel will be an important ingredient in making &aBiosteel, &ras well as powering the &aBio Generator."
		""
		"Alternatively, you can also craft wheat into this nice little brick of &epacked wheat, &rwhich for all intents and purposes is the same as the Biofuel cake. You can make one type or both, whichever floats your boat."
	]
	quest.7AAA9B58C5C9FBFC.quest_subtitle: "No, it's NOT CHEESE"
	quest.7AAA9B58C5C9FBFC.title: "Yellow (and red) Cake"
	quest.7ACD3AA107F04864.quest_desc: ["Using your new plastic sheets, Adamant ingots, and Enderic Compound, you can create this &3Sparkly Thingy!&r As a crafting ingredient, it can be used to create a &alarger&r energy storage, a &anew tier of Core, &ba superconducting Energy Cable&r, and &esomething that goes BOOM.&r You can also use it to capture small, intelligent, magical, flying creatures..."]
	quest.7ACD3AA107F04864.quest_subtitle: "My favorite one is Twist."
	quest.7ACD3AA107F04864.title: "Bejeweled"
	quest.7B0FC4944EA76096.quest_subtitle: "AKA The Movie Nobody Saw"
	quest.7B0FC4944EA76096.title: "Strange World"
	quest.7B20F51A8D079226.quest_desc: ["&bSuperconductors&r in real life are materials that can be cooled to &9EXTREMELY COLD temperatures, &rwhich means they conduct electricity REALLY WELL. In &4Gregtech,&r Superconductors would allow you to route electrical power without losing any due to resistance, &5but in this mod&r they'll allow you to transfer a &aMASSIVE amount of electricity,&r REALLY QUICKLY. Oh, and these &4won't&r connect to regular cables."]
	quest.7B20F51A8D079226.quest_subtitle: "0 degrees Kelvin, that is."
	quest.7B20F51A8D079226.title: "I'm 0K"
	quest.7CA23459D3427F9E.quest_subtitle: "360 Smoke It"
	quest.7CA23459D3427F9E.title: "Blaze Dispensiary"
	quest.7CF4F00CA3B3E572.quest_desc: [
		"Need to rearrange the workshop? Or perhaps you misplaced a machine? &aCarry On's got your back!"
		""
		"By pressing &6shift + right-click&r, you can pick up anything that's considered an entity or tile entity (i.e. animals, chests, machines, etc). Then, you can right-click to place down what you're holding."
	]
	quest.7CF4F00CA3B3E572.quest_subtitle: "and Carry On"
	quest.7D08549E65A25EE8.quest_subtitle: "Cover Yourself in Oil"
	quest.7D08549E65A25EE8.title: "Step 1"
	quest.7D27C6A2F172CA26.quest_subtitle: "HACK HACK COUGH COUGH"
	quest.7D27C6A2F172CA26.title: "Black Lung"
	quest.7DCD2158051FB89E.quest_desc: ["Once you've got your &8Plastic&r and &7Silicon, &ryou can make a battery. On their own, batteries don't really do anything, but they are a necessary crafting ingredient in &6portable energy storage units."]
	quest.7DCD2158051FB89E.quest_subtitle: "I'm suing you"
	quest.7DCD2158051FB89E.title: "Assault and Battery"
	quest.7E7A383EE9519D89.quest_subtitle: "We've cooked."
	quest.7E7A383EE9519D89.title: "99% Pure"
	quest.7F3B8C4FBD610B76.quest_desc: [
		"That's pretty much all the onboarding stuff you need to know. To jump right into the tech tree, just use the chapter navigator at the left of your screen. You can either get started on building your automation empire, or you can take a peek at the automation challenges."
		""
		"&zBest of luck, engineer!&r"
	]
	quest.7F3B8C4FBD610B76.quest_subtitle: "Join the Automation Nation!"
	quest.7F994815F4099139.quest_desc: [
		"This little black blob is...confusing."
		""
		"In real life, Silicon and Silicone are two different things. &aSilicon &ris a shiny metal that's most widely used as a &5superconductor,&r and is the heart of nearly every electronic device out there. The mod author clearly knew this, because Silicon is made using quartz and sand, just like in real life."
		""
		"&4Silicone&r is a rubbery material that is certainly MADE with Silicon, but it also contains other things like carbon and hydrogen. It's very soft and squishy, and is used in a wide variety of fluid and non-fluid applications."
		""
		"Here's where the confusion happens: The texture of Silicon makes me think of &oSilicone Rubber, &ras do the uses (in machines that transport and use fluids, or as the bouncy bottom of the exo-boots). However, the crafting process (as well as the fact that it can be turned into a Silicon Wafer) involves sand and quartz. The two are not interchangeable, as in you cannot use silicone rubber to make a computer chip, and you can't use raw silicon as a fluid gasket."
		""
		"Rant Over."
	]
	quest.7F994815F4099139.quest_subtitle: "I feel like the modmaker confused \"Silicon\" with \"Silicone\""
	quest.7F994815F4099139.title: "Silicon Valley"
